{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts","id":489043,"title":"Second Edition Beasts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-22T22:08:42-07:00","id":489043,"title":"Second Edition Beasts","content":"Oh hey. There's a thing.<br /> <br /> Beasts for Second Edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-beasts/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-beasts/\" target=\"_blank\"> Changeling the Lost Second Edition: Beasts &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-beasts/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-beasts/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":70,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","user":"MachineIV","date":". 04-23-2015, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T22:45:23-07:00","id":489073,"title":"","content":"Very nice! I like the new direction the Blessing and Curse is going, better evoking the image of a being that doesn't want to go <i>back</i>, whatever &quot;back&quot; is. I also like that you can now play the Wise Owl or Sly Fox and still be a Beast rather than some other Seeming with a beast-like look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T23:07:34-07:00","id":489088,"title":"","content":"Ooh, nice to see the shape Blessings and Curses have taken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T23:11:46-07:00","id":489089,"title":"","content":"Very nice, but now it has me wondering about things like how Clarity works in 2e :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T23:21:17-07:00","id":489099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=489089#post489089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very nice, but now it has me wondering about things like how Clarity works in 2e :P</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a whole other animal. I plan to make it a little more fluid, FWIW. But we're focusing heavily on &quot;Clarity&quot;, and the experience and perception of being Lost. I'll probably tease it sooner than later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T23:23:46-07:00","id":489100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=489099#post489099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a whole other animal. I plan to make it a little more fluid, FWIW. But we're focusing heavily on &quot;Clarity&quot;, and the experience and perception of being Lost. I'll probably tease it sooner than later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking forward to that!<br /> <br /> Otherwise, like I said, the beast writeup itself is awesome, and I agree with the happiness about being able to play a mentally focused character like a clever cat or wise owl type as a Beast, without being mechanically penalized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T01:59:04-07:00","id":489154,"title":"","content":"I thought the Beast seeming was unnecessary, and it was a bad idea to keep it. This changed my mind, but I'm concerned at how Ogres will be different from Beasts. My only suggestion would be to clearly differentiate the two, if they both exist. I'm interested in seeing how the components are implemented in other Seemings. It is difficult for me to judge them in a vacuum. The Beast Seeming seems to do the job it is meant to do. I'll try to wrap my brain around how some of the more exotic Kiths could be implemented with the Beast Seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T06:50:26-07:00","id":489426,"title":"","content":"I don't imagine differentiating Ogres will be hard.<br /> <br /> The entire write up is sexy as hell, per Second Edition's trends. Blessing and Curses in particular are ingenious ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T06:57:59-07:00","id":489432,"title":"","content":"I really like where they took the shift of symbolism in the Seemings. Making the Curse and the Blessing this intimately related to <i>who</i> and <i>what</i> the Seeming made the Changeling is inspired as heck too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T07:36:10-07:00","id":489447,"title":"","content":"Also, while I'm going to need some more about it, an innate ability to escape bonds is a great addition to a changeling's inherent bag of escapologist's tricks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T08:03:54-07:00","id":489493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=489154#post489154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the Beast seeming was unnecessary, and it was a bad idea to keep it. This changed my mind, but I'm concerned at how Ogres will be different from Beasts. My only suggestion would be to clearly differentiate the two, if they both exist. I'm interested in seeing how the components are implemented in other Seemings. It is difficult for me to judge them in a vacuum. The Beast Seeming seems to do the job it is meant to do. I'll try to wrap my brain around how some of the more exotic Kiths could be implemented with the Beast Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div> Doesn't seem like too much of an issue. Ogres were all about violence and the cycle of abuse last edition; I think that could easily be parlayed into the next edition. <br /> <br /> I like the new twist on the Beasts; at the very least, I'm interested in how you do Elemental, since that seems equally hard to do in the new paradigm(though I'm hoping we get to keep the &quot;inhumanity&quot;/&quot;alienation&quot; themes).<br /> <br /> And, maybe this is just me, but there's a 7th Seeming?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T08:28:58-07:00","id":489511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=489493#post489493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Doesn't seem like too much of an issue. Ogres were all about violence and the cycle of abuse last edition; I think that could easily be parlayed into the next edition.<br /> <br /> I like the new twist on the Beasts; at the very least, I'm interested in how you do Elemental, since that seems equally hard to do in the new paradigm(though I'm hoping we get to keep the &quot;inhumanity&quot;/&quot;alienation&quot; themes).<br /> <br /> And, maybe this is just me, but there's a 7th Seeming?!</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like the Seemings will continue the theme of ways to (mentally) surive and react to abuse (though not the necessarily healthy ways). Changeling is a game about surviving and overcoming abuse or ordeals after all. So if Ogres are violence and the cycle of abuse, and Beast is losing and finding yourself in the primal emotions, then Elemental should be dissociation, detachement from the self that underwent the trauma. So an Draconic Kith changling, when becoming Elemental , turns into a dragon made of stone, becoming detached and impervious to harm.<br /> <br /> I think it is very important that this part of Changleing remains integral, it is the heart of the game and what sets it apart from the other gamelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1228-jhiriit","name":"Jhiriit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T10:39:24-07:00","id":489643,"title":"","content":"if you ever make a poll to what Seeming to do next put one vote to Fairest","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T13:28:07-07:00","id":489780,"title":"","content":"This is just complete speculation here, and I am sorry if it sounds stupid.<br /> <br /> What if the 7th Seeming represents Agency in two ways?<br /> <br /> In the first sub-Seeming, you took Agency by embracing Imperfection. More so than a human, you do not let exacerbated Vices, naive Virtues and unrealistic Aspirations rule you. Unlike the Gentry, you do not wear a mask of an angel or demon. The Blessing is <span style=\"font-size:18px\">&quot;Human, All Too Human&quot;:</span> once per story, you may automatically get an Exceptional Success on a roll to convince someone to find balance. Whenever you reach an Aspiration related to your flaws, take two Beats instead of one. The Curse is, believe it or not, <span style=\"font-size:18px\">&quot;Do As You Will&quot;:</span> at least once per story, your character will be forced to make decisions with two extreme outcomes, you stubbornly try to find a middle ground that is simply not possible. Assume that whether your character is forced to make a choice or does it of his own volition, the final result is much less impressive than it could be otherwise (Exceptional Success becomes Success, Success becomes Failure and Failure becomes Dramatic Failure).<br /> <br /> In the second sub-Seeming, you took Agency by striving towards Perfection. More so than a normal changeling, you focus your Vices, Virtues and Aspirations into sources of great power. Unlike the Fae, you truly take others into account as more than extensions of your whims: they are fire forged friends and respectable rivals. The Blessing is <span style=\"font-size:18px\">&quot;Fae, Wondrously Fae&quot;: </span>once per story, when you fulfill your Virtue, you regain all glamour points. Alternatively you may fulfill your vice to regain 50% of your maximum glamour, round up. When you reach an Aspiration related to approaching your idea of perfection, take two Beats instead of one. The Curse is <span style=\"font-size:18px\">&quot;Larger Than Life&quot;: <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">at once</span></span></span> per story, the Wyrd offers an opportunity to find the perfect middle ground for a conflict. Whether your character is forced into finding the middle ground or goes after it himself, the final result is less grandiose than he would like (same as the Curse above).<br /> <br /> This Seeming could be called <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Seeker. </span>Those who belong to this Seeming can change what they Seek, but this is best done through play instead of rolls. Some seek balance, some seek greatness in either direction. Both have flaws the other does not have. I know it's kind of cheating to have a double Seeming, but I still think it would be cool and I would use it.<br /> <br /> Example: Draconic kith with the Seeker Seeming could be a wise mentor like a Chinese Dragon, helping settle disputes and advising rulers. A Draconic kith with the same Seeming could an ambitious destroyer, like an European Dragon, conquering most foes and desires, but showing true respect for Knights that challenge him (nobly or begrudgingly on either side).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-23-2015, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T13:28:30-07:00","id":489781,"title":"","content":"Alright! Changeling stuff!<br /> <br /> Something I find very interesting about how Seemings are being handled is that they are almost scars in and of themselves. When the chips were down, you did what you had to do to survive but it turns out &quot;what you had to do to survive&quot; might not be something you would (or even should) be proud of. I'm actually really impressed by this and think it has a lot of potential if the other Seemings can match this tone. Yes they're expressions of agency, but that doesn't mean they aren't traumatic in their own right. They're another part of the entire experience of being Lost that the character has to come to terms with.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T17:13:44-07:00","id":490075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=489780#post489780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is just complete speculation here, and I am sorry if it sounds stupid.<br /> <br /> What if the 7th Seeming represents Agency in two ways?<br /> <br /> In the first sub-Seeming, you took Agency by embracing Imperfection. More so than a human, you do not let exacerbated Vices, naive Virtues and unrealistic Aspirations rule you. Unlike the Gentry, you do not wear a mask of an angel or demon. The Blessing is <span style=\"font-size:18px\">&quot;Human, All Too Human&quot;:</span> once per story, you may automatically get an Exceptional Success on a roll to convince someone to find balance. Whenever you reach an Aspiration related to your flaws, take two Beats instead of one. The Curse is, believe it or not, <span style=\"font-size:18px\">&quot;Do As You Will&quot;:</span> at least once per story, your character will be forced to make decisions with two extreme outcomes, you stubbornly try to find a middle ground that is simply not possible. Assume that whether your character is forced to make a choice or does it of his own volition, the final result is much less impressive than it could be otherwise (Exceptional Success becomes Success, Success becomes Failure and Failure becomes Dramatic Failure).<br /> <br /> In the second sub-Seeming, you took Agency by striving towards Perfection. More so than a normal changeling, you focus your Vices, Virtues and Aspirations into sources of great power. Unlike the Fae, you truly take others into account as more than extensions of your whims: they fire forged friends and respectable rivals. The Blessing is <span style=\"font-size:18px\">&quot;Fae, Wondrously Fae&quot;: </span>once per story, when you fulfill your Virtue, you regain all glamour points. Alternatively you may fulfill your vice to regain 50% of your maximum glamour, round up. When you reach an Aspiration related approaching your idea of perfection, take two Beats instead of one. The Curse is <span style=\"font-size:18px\">&quot;Larger Than Life&quot;: <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">at once</span></span></span> per story, the Wyrd offers an opportunity to find the perfect middle ground for a conflict. Whether your character is forced into finding the middle ground or goes after it himself, the final result is less grandiose than he would like (same as the Curse above).<br /> <br /> This Seeming could be called <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Seeker. </span>Those who belong to this Seeming can change what they Seek, but this is best done through play instead of rolls. Some seek balance, some seek greatness in either direction. Both have flaws the other does not have. I know it's kind of cheating to have a double Seeming, but I still think it would be cool and I would use it.<br /> <br /> Example: Draconic kith the Seeker Seeming could be a wise mentor like a Chinese Dragon, helping settle disputes and advising rulers. A Draconic kith with the same Seeming could an ambitious destroyer, like an European Dragon, conquering most foes and desires, but showing true respect for Knights that challenge him (nobly or begrudgingly on either side).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really cool foundation for a Seeming. <br /> <br /> Well then. <br /> <br /> I actually have an idea for an eighth apocryphal Seeming. But I may or may not have room for it down the line. It can't fit in the core book, or REDACTED.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T17:41:59-07:00","id":490086,"title":"","content":"Let me get this straight, now Kith comes first and Seeming second in character creation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5775-periculum","name":"Periculum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T17:43:45-07:00","id":490090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Periculum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=490086#post490086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me get this straight, now Kith comes first and Seeming second in character creation?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep! Your Kith is what you did/were in Arcadia, Seeming how you escaped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T18:13:43-07:00","id":490099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=490090#post490090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yep! Your Kith is what you did/were in Arcadia, Seeming how you escaped.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> From the sound of it, I'm guessing that any Changeling can now possess any Kith, which is pretty cool. And we're going to have over 100 of them! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T18:20:03-07:00","id":490103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=489154#post489154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the Beast seeming was unnecessary, and it was a bad idea to keep it. This changed my mind, but I'm concerned at how Ogres will be different from Beasts. My only suggestion would be to clearly differentiate the two, if they both exist. I'm interested in seeing how the components are implemented in other Seemings. It is difficult for me to judge them in a vacuum. The Beast Seeming seems to do the job it is meant to do. I'll try to wrap my brain around how some of the more exotic Kiths could be implemented with the Beast Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I thought Beasts were a good idea, since a pretty sizeable number of fairy tales involve animals. But the difference between the two from what I've been able to gather is that Beasts are feral and primitive, where as Ogres are sentient but also brutal. When a Beast mauls somebody, it's because that is in their nature to do so. When an Ogre mauls somebody, it's probably because you pissed them off.<br /> <br /> Beasts escaped by resorting to their animal instincts, but since Ogres are known for their strength and brutishness, I'm guessing that they escaped by cracking the skulls of anybody who stood in their way. One day they've had enough of the whips and the insults and the 200 lbs crates strapped to their backs and decide to just bash their way to freedom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T18:44:54-07:00","id":490119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=490099#post490099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> From the sound of it, I'm guessing that any Changeling can now possess any Kith, which is pretty cool. And we're going to have over 100 of them! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. Kith came first in your experience. You got your role to play in Arcadia. Seeming bends, warps, and owns it. Seeming makes that Kith yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T18:46:52-07:00","id":490121,"title":"","content":"Many thanks for the preview! ^_^ I've been really looking forward to learning more about 2e.<br /> <br /> I really like the idea of the Seeming Blessing and Curse connecting with Clarity. I'll be interested to see the Clarity preview you mentioned, when it's ready. I'm also interested in learning more about innate Changeling abilities, like that ease of slipping past mundane constraints.<br /> <br /> Ah, also, a question. I think it may have been asked before, but I'm not sure what answer it got, or if it got one. How strongly does the game tie the aesthetics of a Changeling's Mien to the Seeming? Can a Beast exhibit no strong animal resemblance (conveying the Seeming more through a distinctly wild impression), and a member of another Seeming display a very pronounced animal appearance? I'm thinking of a couple of 1e Beast characters whose aesthetics I liked, but the 2e Beast Seeming doesn't look like a good fit for them.<br /> <br /> On thinking about it, it's interesting to look at the Seeming now relative to the last edition. Going by the 1e book, Beasts generally secured their freedoms by clawing their ways back from instinct, while in 2e they secured their freedom by diving into it. The &quot;base&quot; narratives are like mirror images of one another. Has that been fairly common thing across the 2e Seemings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T20:12:09-07:00","id":490156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=490119#post490119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct. Kith came first in your experience. You got your role to play in Arcadia. Seeming bends, warps, and owns it. Seeming makes that Kith yours.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I was thinking of maybe buying Beast as the next book, but this drew me back to Changeling! :P<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, now I can fulfill my fantasy of an Ogre (brewer) who slogged his way through the Hedge in a drunken brawl!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-23-2015, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T20:28:44-07:00","id":490163,"title":"","content":"I suddenly have an idea for a spider-beast who's like a changeling Banksy, except instead of graffiti he constructs massively intricate &quot;webs&quot; out of string or tape..!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T21:10:34-07:00","id":490174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=490103#post490103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the difference between the two from what I've been able to gather is that Beasts are feral and primitive, where as Ogres are sentient but also brutal. When a Beast mauls somebody, it's because that is in their nature to do so. When an Ogre mauls somebody, it's probably because you pissed them off.<br /> <br /> Beasts escaped by resorting to their animal instincts, but since Ogres are known for their strength and brutishness, I'm guessing that they escaped by cracking the skulls of anybody who stood in their way. One day they've had enough of the whips and the insults and the 200 lbs crates strapped to their backs and decide to just bash their way to freedom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with this reading, unless you meant it as a 1e reading.<br /> <br /> It sounds to me that 2e Beasts aren't about instinct; they're about breaking taboos. They've perceived a specific type of bondage as the quintessential prison and have broken out of it. Instinct is certainly a possible alternative to the civilized response, but it's not the <i>only</i> possible alternative. The wizard's tower comes to mind.<br /> <br /> Granted, that reading makes it a lot harder for me to speculate about 2e Ogres and how they're distinct from 2e Beasts, so... I've probably got it wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T21:24:36-07:00","id":490183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=490174#post490174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree with this reading, unless you meant it as a 1e reading.<br /> <br /> It sounds to me that 2e Beasts aren't about instinct; they're about breaking taboos. They've perceived a specific type of bondage as the quintessential prison and have broken out of it. Instinct is certainly a possible alternative to the civilized response, but it's not the <i>only</i> possible alternative. The wizard's tower comes to mind.<br /> <br /> Granted, that reading makes it a lot harder for me to speculate about 2e Ogres and how they're distinct from 2e Beasts, so... I've probably got it wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well it says they rejected the civilized world and embraced the beast within. They also gain back clarity from doing something that is socially unacceptable, like say pissing on your front door to make sure everybody knows that's your territory! I think it mentioned clawing and biting during the escape attempt, which seems pretty in touch with instincts to me. I don't think being uncultured is going to really help you escape your cage, but lashing out with claws and fangs might.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T00:10:42-07:00","id":490277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=490183#post490183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well it says they rejected the civilized world and embraced the beast within. They also gain back clarity from doing something that is socially unacceptable, like say pissing on your front door to make sure everybody knows that's your territory! I think it mentioned clawing and biting during the escape attempt, which seems pretty in touch with instincts to me. I don't think being uncultured is going to really help you escape your cage, but lashing out with claws and fangs might.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Errol said, instinct is a valid expression of it, but what's been described really is broader than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Escape</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">She already knows what it feels like to be without choices, to submit, to lean on humanity and civility. After all, that way failed her as her situation went from bad to worse in the hands of her Keeper. So she makes a choice, she chooses to do something wild, something socially unacceptable, something animalistic. She bites through flesh, claws through soil, smears herself with shit and blood to escape the Huntsman on her heels. She chooses to break a taboo, destroys her civility, and in making that choice, she escapes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note all that taboo stuff she's doing. The emphasis is on how it's something she <i>chooses</i> to do, not something instinct <i>compels</i> her to do. She's very much in control. She's just made the decision that if behaving in a socially acceptable, civilized fashion is going to deny her options that might actually get her out, then fuck that noise.<br /> <br /> That attitude carries through to the other side of her Durance. The emphasis is always on freedom,* especially freedom from societal standards of propriety. She doesn't let those standards get in the way of doing what she wants to do how it seems best to her to do them. This in no way means (by default) that what she wants to do is indulge in instinctual animalistic behavior. Animalistic behavior is simply deemed an acceptable means to an end, where applicable -- it got her out, after all -- but not the end itself.<br /> <br /> * The idea of pushing the boundaries on what she can do skill-wise was a nice touch, I thought.<br /> <br /> This is why the Beast's Blessing involves flaunting cultural taboos: it's so self-affirming to remind herself how little hold the ever-present chains of societal pressure have on what she does that she's willing to risk a high price to prove it. Like, the first comment on the blog post includes an example of a fox girl taking a selfie in front of a bunch of meth. I mean... Daaaaamn, would she have earned that Clarity. No animalistic instinct in play, there. ... Now, it's kind of an unfortunate see-saw that getting caught means imprisonment, and the resulting breaking point might take that Clarity right back, but hey! XD<br /> <br /> Again, &quot;acting on animal instinct&quot; isn't a bad way to play a Beast, but it's important to recognize that it's a circle within a larger circle labeled &quot;violating cultural taboos&quot; in the Venn diagram.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T02:06:25-07:00","id":490348,"title":"","content":"What's 'REDACTED'. Is that the name of a book? Or something that was edited out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T02:58:49-07:00","id":490366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wildfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=490348#post490348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's 'REDACTED'. Is that the name of a book? Or something that was edited out?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a thing I'm not talking about yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T05:41:49-07:00","id":490428,"title":"","content":"The Beast preview is reassuring, given the earlier discussion about Seemings (and how Beasts/Elementals were harder to move to &quot;how you escaped&quot; than Darklings, Fairest, Ogres, or Wizened). I'm not completely sold on how it'll be distinct from Ogres, but there's a lot of ways it could go.<br /> <br /> I'm also really liking the implication that Changelings have an innate break-out-of-bonds power (a la early Separation contracts, but for everyone). Although I predict that power gets nullified if the Changeling is bound by cold iron or something (there's a number of stories where a faerie can only be held in bonds of iron).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T07:04:55-07:00","id":490495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=490428#post490428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Beast preview is reassuring, given the earlier discussion about Seemings (and how Beasts/Elementals were harder to move to &quot;how you escaped&quot; than Darklings, Fairest, Ogres, or Wizened). I'm not completely sold on how it'll be distinct from Ogres, but there's a lot of ways it could go.<br /> <br /> I'm also really liking the implication that Changelings have an innate break-out-of-bonds power (a la early Separation contracts, but for everyone). Although I predict that power gets nullified if the Changeling is bound by cold iron or something (there's a number of stories where a faerie can only be held in bonds of iron).</div> </div> </div> </div>Iron will suffice, yes. <br /> <br /> And I THINK Ogres are going to be focused on consumption. I think. I haven't read Filamena's draft of it yet, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T10:19:28-07:00","id":490660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=490495#post490495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I THINK Ogres are going to be focused on consumption. I think. I haven't read Filamena's draft of it yet, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>/blink<br /> <br /> ...and it clicks. This works for me. There's still overlap, but it's not a complete overlap, which makes it work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T10:54:28-07:00","id":490717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=490075#post490075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a really cool foundation for a Seeming.<br /> <br /> Well then.<br /> <br /> I actually have an idea for an eighth apocryphal Seeming. But I may or may not have room for it down the line. It can't fit in the core book, or REDACTED.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could also work as a Court - the feeling of Failure and using your flaws to remind yourself of Humanity","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T16:29:00-07:00","id":491057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=490717#post490717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It could also work as a Court - the feeling of Failure and using your flaws to remind yourself of Humanity</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah. <br /> <br /> My eighth is unrelated. Two completely separate thoughts. <br /> <br /> But yes. That'd make a neato Court.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T16:50:23-07:00","id":491073,"title":"","content":"I thought on the Elemental from this,(although my version might have a name change.) <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The Elemental made a choice. To give up the short, lesser bursts of everyday anxieties and emotion. To give up all that, in return for the ever immortality of stone. When the Keeper can no longer get a response from its... prior torture victim, it leaves, unsure what else to say. And so she left, without a trace, for her human was gone, for the quiet power of everlasting stone.&quot;<br /> <br /> To be fair, the above is more like a Kith, but, its a thought I had dealing with their alien nature. Essentially, that alienation means you stop responding to traditional stimuli and hence, you stop being, &quot;fun,&quot; for the Keeper. <br /> <br /> This version has many issues, of course, but, its a thought. <br /> <br /> <br /> On another note, this was awesome! It answers all the fears I had about how the Beast was going to work out, and does quite a bit to shine a light on how the book is going to proceed. <br /> <br /> More!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T19:18:47-07:00","id":491178,"title":"","content":"That makes sense, they looked inside themselves and found they resonate with a certain element. By drawing upon that connection, they found the strength to endure the hardships of Arcadia, and eventually managed to escape.<br /> <br /> It's like Bruce Lee said &quot;Be water, my friend!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T19:48:12-07:00","id":491187,"title":"","content":"Beasts abandon the World and embrace the Self. <br /> Elementals abandon the Self and embrace the World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T20:01:27-07:00","id":491193,"title":"","content":"Anyone else thought this was about Beast: The Primodial vs. Changeling when they first read the thread title?<br /> <br /> Anyways love the Seeming, but it occurs to me that particapating in S&amp;M could trigger both curse and blessing at the same time (if submissive). Your confined physically, but also breaking a societial taboo.<br /> <br /> One question, does agreeing to any magical pledge count as confining and invoke the curse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T20:06:37-07:00","id":491197,"title":"","content":"Probably not, since you have to enter that willingly for it to take affect. Also, I believe they pointed out that it applies to mundane confinement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T15:33:02-07:00","id":492039,"title":"","content":"Bit of a side note, but I'm also curious which Kiths will be getting merged. Right now all that spring to mind are Swimmerskins (formerly Beasts) and Water-Dwellers (formerly Ogres) since they both fall under &quot;Stuff that lives in water.&quot; Most of the other stuff is built around fairly distinct concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T15:36:47-07:00","id":492043,"title":"","content":"That is a subject of curiosity, actually. Between Ocean Born, Swimmer Skin and Water-Dwellers, we've got at least 3 aquatic themed Kiths. If they're planning to merge the similar ones and still have 100 in the core book alone, that's going to be impressive. If, however, they're leaving them separate, then there may be multiple variations of similar Kiths depending on the roles you were given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T15:49:36-07:00","id":492055,"title":"","content":"I don't really count Waterborn with those two since they're <i>literally</i> water and the other two are just things that live in it. It'd be like fusing Bird-kith (I forget the name) and Airtouched because they both involve the sky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T15:58:23-07:00","id":492057,"title":"","content":"True, but as they explained previously, your <i>kith comes before</i> your seeming this time around. So you don't become an Elemental until your escape. Your Kith comes first, but your Seeming makes the Kith yours in a personal way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T16:10:39-07:00","id":492063,"title":"","content":"Right but Kiths are still your durance. The difference now is that you can be a living flame or water in a pond or a cloud or w/e and not be tied to the Elemental seeming. That doesn't change the fact that your durance had you living as an object. So that split between you were aquatic vs you were aqua would still matter. Same with birds and sky or moleperson and dirtperson. Its the same way the Beast seeming is now separate from the &quot;Beast&quot; kiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T16:17:47-07:00","id":492065,"title":"","content":"Dave gives an early list from a ways back. Some may have been added,* and some may have been found to be distinct enough after all.<br /> <br /> * Truefriend and Playmate seem like strong candidates for merging, for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings?p=396910#post396910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Windwing/Lurkglider</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Stonebones/Earthbones</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\">Cleareyes/Cyclopean </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Hunterheart/</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Razorhand</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\">Palewraith/Shadowsoul</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\">Waterborn/Swimmerskin</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\">Succubus/Romancer</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\">I think there are maybe some others; these were just from the first list brought up. But, these might be cases where you get one as the main kith, and one is just an example Seeming variant on it. Or something. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=492055#post492055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really count Waterborn with those two since they're <i>literally</i> water and the other two are just things that live in it. It'd be like fusing Bird-kith (I forget the name) and Airtouched because they both involve the sky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, depends on the point of emphasis. 1e Waterborn and 1e Swimmerskin really were just different takes on, &quot;better at swimming and not drowning,&quot; when you get down to it. Now, there are probably more interesting things to do with having a body that's literally made of water, though time will tell if they'll capitalize on it. They're tight on space, remember.<br /> <br /> That said, there was also this from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline\">the outline</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The 2e Changeling: The Lost Outline</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kith blessings need to be a) pretty universally useful, b) pretty fearsome, and c) interesting. They can be double-faceted, if you\u2019ve got something weird like a waterbreathing kith. So they could breathe water, AND have something generally useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T16:51:17-07:00","id":492098,"title":"","content":"I can already imagine an Ogre made of living water as this hulking, mouthless creature with a torrent of water in place of legs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T17:13:47-07:00","id":492107,"title":"","content":"A Satyr which could be a Romancer of the Beast Seeming. <br /> <br /> I'm really looking forward to seeing the other Seemings.<br /> <br /> I mean as I understand it a Darkling sacrifices the light within themselves to escape, Orgers have to do with consumption (but how consumption adds escaping I don't know).<br /> <br /> Fairest my guess embrace social interaction to escape, you talk your way out. An ability to regain clarity based on a social nteraction, while the curse would be social isolation. Just a guess.<br /> <br /> Wizen you embrace your skills/training. Blessing could be using your skills to do something major. Curse breaking a tool.<br /> <br /> .Elemental, rejection of emotions, using pure logic to escape. Blessing could be when you reject an emotional response gain a point of Clarity. Curse, an emotional break down costs point of Clarity.<br /> <br /> Darklings, sacrificing the light within, could be literal, could be figurately. I remember the scarificing the light thing somewhere I think. Could be scarificing something or someone you love. It means your connection to other people. Blessing hiding/isolation, could be literal hiding or isolating from other via lies or something like that. Curse, leaving your self exposed, like telling someone a.secret.<br /> <br /> Orgers are another hard guess, but we have a hint, consumption. hmmm, they ate they're way out, used the local resources? Blessing, over endulgence to regain a point of clarity. Curse, temperence,.fasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 04-25-2015, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T17:46:29-07:00","id":492122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=492107#post492107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Satyr which could be a Romancer of the Beast Seeming.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;They're a wet dream come true when aroused. Which is often.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Works for me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T01:22:22-07:00","id":492432,"title":"","content":"Satyr being a beast romancer works on multiple levels, Satyr's tend to reject civilization in myths and fiction, tend to violate taboos, and have animal parts, so the beast part fits, and Satyr's tend to be all about sex so the Romancer fits as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T03:20:03-07:00","id":492482,"title":"","content":"Hehe, I play a Satyr looking changeling currently who is a Darkling, mainly I didn't think any of the Beast kith fit it and I felt having animal ken to goats would be pretty silly... Gotta say, I wasn't sure at first when I first saw this new Beast outline, but I'm liking how each of the Seemings are now dealing with the method of escape along with partly how your character's changeling mien manifests... I really like that change. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I can see me struggling over what Kith will make the most interesting character though... 100+? Wow. And I take it any Seeming can pick any Kith now too? So much choices...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T07:30:30-07:00","id":492571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=492432#post492432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satyr being a beast romancer works on multiple levels, Satyr's tend to reject civilization in myths and fiction, tend to violate taboos, and have animal parts, so the beast part fits, and Satyr's tend to be all about sex so the Romancer fits as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Which makes you wonder what the hell Mr. Tomnus was planning to do when he invited Lucy back to his home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T09:04:33-07:00","id":492621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=492065#post492065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, depends on the point of emphasis. 1e Waterborn and 1e Swimmerskin really were just different takes on, &quot;better at swimming and not drowning,&quot; when you get down to it. Now, there are probably more interesting things to do with having a body that's literally made of water, though time will tell if they'll capitalize on it. They're tight on space, remember.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah like I could see a fishperson being good at swimming vs a waterperson being good at escaping grapples or melding with bodies of water or something. Most of the other merges on that list make sense, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T09:33:19-07:00","id":492659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=492571#post492571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Which makes you wonder what the hell Mr. Tomnus was planning to do when he invited Lucy back to his home.</div> </div> </div> </div> He was a Faun, thank you very much! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T12:39:33-07:00","id":492801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=492621#post492621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah like I could see a fishperson being good at swimming vs a waterperson being good at escaping grapples or melding with bodies of water or something. Most of the other merges on that list make sense, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we need to keep Contracts in mind here. Kith is what you were turned into; Seemings are how you took your power back. But Seemings also dictate Contract Affinities.<br /> <br /> If you were made into a being that lives in water (Aquatic Kith), your Seeming is going to influence your Contracts and further ways that expresses itself. A Beast's Contracts can focus on being more capable of physical things, while an Elemental's Contracts can be more literal about &quot;being water.&quot;<br /> <br /> As well, this also gets around any weird things like air, sand, or other fluid Elementals that would make sense to have escaping, or melding, powers looking at the &quot;made of water&quot; Kith over Kiths that deal with their Elements and letting their Contracts deal with such things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T15:21:06-07:00","id":492969,"title":"","content":"I'm... Just... Having a hard time wrapping my head around the idea of 100 Kiths in the core book alone... Like, holy crap, is there going to be room for anything else in the book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T15:32:51-07:00","id":492975,"title":"","content":"100 Kiths x 5 Seemings means 500 possible combinations. More choices in Courts as well. 600 when Seeming/Kith combos when the 6th Seeming comes out in redacted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T16:08:25-07:00","id":492983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=492975#post492975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">100 Kiths x 5 Seemings means 500 possible combinations. More choices in Courts as well. 600 when Seeming/Kith combos when the 6th Seeming comes out in redacted.</div> </div> </div> </div>x 4 Courts means 2,000 combinations out of the box, 2,400 with redacted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T17:43:24-07:00","id":493055,"title":"","content":"Given that 2e is supposed to come with more customizable Courts and the expectation that most games will use one of a set of sample Courts, or make their own, that number is probably going to be even higher once the book is finished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T17:55:39-07:00","id":493057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=492969#post492969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm... Just... Having a hard time wrapping my head around the idea of 100 Kiths in the core book alone... Like, holy crap, is there going to be room for anything else in the book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Kiths really don't require much space at all, wordcount-wise. They clock in at just under 20,000 words for all 100.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T17:59:52-07:00","id":493062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=493055#post493055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that 2e is supposed to come with more customizable Courts and the expectation that most games will use one of a set of sample Courts, or make their own, that number is probably going to be even higher once the book is finished.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yeah. We'll have sample Courts. But Court Creation is going to be a thing we encourage. I don't know how many individual Courts each sample city will have, so I can't tell you what kind of combination that'd make for yet. <br /> <br /> But the 500 estimate up there is off. Remember, six Seemings, 100 Kiths. So that's a base 600. Even if you consider that some characters might not have a Seeming. <br /> <br /> REDACTED will give us another 100~ combinations. (And just to tease you all, REDACTED is actually Dark Eras. The Grimm's Fairy Tales Dark Era will have a new, Second Edition compliant Seeming.) <br /> <br /> If I get the chance to do my eighth Seeming, it'll add similarly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T18:43:22-07:00","id":493109,"title":"","content":"I deem these numbers appropriate for a game that focuses on dreams and imagination!<br /> <br /> <br /> But have you considered the possibilities of dual kith combinations? Have fun with that, math wizards!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T18:43:58-07:00","id":493110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=493062#post493062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yeah. We'll have sample Courts. But Court Creation is going to be a thing we encourage. I don't know how many individual Courts each sample city will have, so I can't tell you what kind of combination that'd make for yet.<br /> <br /> But the 500 estimate up there is off. Remember, six Seemings, 100 Kiths. So that's a base 600. Even if you consider that some characters might not have a Seeming.<br /> <br /> REDACTED will give us another 100~ combinations. (And just to tease you all, <b>REDACTED is actually Dark Eras. The Grimm's Fairy Tales Dark Era will have a new, Second Edition compliant Seeming.</b>)<br /> <br /> If I get the chance to do my eighth Seeming, it'll add similarly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that's awesome news! ^__^<br /> <br /> One question relating to Seemings; With the changes brought to Seemings and Kith, will the Contracts actually still be reliant on Seeming choice as ones a changeling is adept or not adept at starting out, or will there be some change? Basically, will Seeming Contracts still exist or not? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T18:52:43-07:00","id":493117,"title":"","content":"In short, it's more than it ever was: If you can't make a character concept in Changeling, you're probably not working hard enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T18:53:12-07:00","id":493119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=493110#post493110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh that's awesome news! ^__^<br /> <br /> One question relating to Seemings; With the changes brought to Seemings and Kith, will the Contracts actually still be reliant on Seeming choice as ones a changeling is adept or not adept at starting out, or will there be some change? Basically, will Seeming Contracts still exist or not? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Seeming will flavour your Contracts. Some Seemings will work better with some Contracts without expanding on them. Some Seemings will probably want to pick up other Seemings' flavours to enhance them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T19:04:02-07:00","id":493129,"title":"","content":"Also;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean as I understand it a Darkling sacrifices the light within themselves to escape </div> </div> </div>If this is true or one of the Seemings has this as their schtick, I'm in. I really like the concept of troubled characters and those with a dark past or ones that carry a shameful secret when it comes to Changeling (Playing a Theon Greyjoy/Reek character in a game like this has quite a bit of potential). It seems to me that a Seeming like that will carry a good bit of character development along with emotional and psychological weight going into a story. Having something like that flavour Contracts and having seemingly (hah!) a wider choice makes me really look forward to the game as it's coming out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T19:14:52-07:00","id":493137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=493057#post493057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Kiths really don't require much space at all, wordcount-wise. They clock in at just under 20,000 words for all 100.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, awesome! I have a feeling Changeling 2e is going to be a lot for me to digest, but I'm definitely looking forward to it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T20:35:43-07:00","id":493188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">To the Changeling eye, the Beast has let the wildness inside out, and remade himself from parts of the wild real and imagined. He may be simply lion on two legs, proud and golden and beautiful. Or he may be parts and pieces, a horn, a maw, dripping bird-talons and snake teeth. Chimera-like Beasts may reflect a conflict between the Kith inflicted on them and the animal soul they claimed for themselves at the time of their escape.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Does this mean that changelings are no longer changed by being in Arcadia and/or by their Keepers? I'm sorry if it's been said elsewhere but I'm behind. =)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T20:58:33-07:00","id":493231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KismetRose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=493188#post493188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does this mean that changelings are no longer changed by being in Arcadia and/or by their Keepers? I'm sorry if it's been said elsewhere but I'm behind. =)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Your question confused me at first, but I think I can answer it now. From what we've been told, your character apparently retains their human form for the majority of their durance, and finally becomes their Seeming during the escape. So, for example, your keeper might treat you like a house pet, but depending on how you escape will determine whether you become a cute kitten (Beast), or a gorgeous sex slave (Fairest), and so on. You're given your job when you come into Arcadia, and you're given your form when you leave.<br /> <br /> Hope I answered that right!</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T21:01:38-07:00","id":493233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KismetRose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=493188#post493188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this mean that changelings are no longer changed by being in Arcadia and/or by their Keepers? I'm sorry if it's been said elsewhere but I'm behind. =)</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Focus in on the &quot;between the Kith inflicted on them&quot; bit. In 1e, a Changeling's Seeming and Kith were both what she was turned into. In 2e, the Kith is still what the character was made into, but the Seeming is a reflection of how the character took back her life. Kiths are evidently also being made more potent.<br /> <br /> You might also feel more up to speed after looking over the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline\">2e outline</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T21:02:20-07:00","id":493237,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Nyrufa. That's about all I needed to know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T22:30:55-07:00","id":493272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=493233#post493233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No worries. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Focus in on the &quot;between the Kith inflicted on them&quot; bit. In 1e, a Changeling's Seeming and Kith were both what she was turned into. In 2e, the Kith is still what the character was made into, but the Seeming is a reflection of how the character took back her life. Kiths are evidently also being made more potent.<br /> <br /> You might also feel more up to speed after looking over the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline\">2e outline</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Gaius said. <br /> <br /> Your Keeper abducts you, and turns you onto your Kith. Your Kith is the role you play in the Durance. When you escape, you flavour the Kith with a Seeming, based on how you took control and fled. So a Keeper might have needed a bunch of dragons. So, he abducts a bunch of Changelings and turns them into Draconic Kiths. But when the group decides to escape, they each choose a different method of escape. That means they're each still Draconic, but of different Seemings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T23:09:13-07:00","id":493308,"title":"","content":"Oh, right. I didn't think about that.<br /> <br /> D:<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry, Kismet, but I think I gave you an inaccurate explanation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T23:38:54-07:00","id":493322,"title":"","content":"Ooh... The way the outline lists the deadlines I may be able to get 2nd edition as a neat birthday present for myself, depending how long it's in Layout before release...<br /> <br /> EDIT = Just read what the Huntsmen are... <i>Wow</i>. <i>That's scary what they can do</i>. I am glad as mentioned before in other threads that there's a reason to actually get into the Hedge and look about now.<br /> <br /> There doesn't seem to be much or any of a wordcount on the Hedge though... Maybe it's split up between Goblin Fruits and Onieromancy rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3951,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","user":"wander","date":". 04-27-2015, 02:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T05:36:51-07:00","id":493498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=492107#post492107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Satyr which could be a Romancer of the Beast Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Actually, that Kith + Seeming could apply to several mythical Beasts such as the Japanese Fox-Wife and the Irish Selkie. Both are magical animals (fox and seal) who disguise themselves as humans and seduce men, even going so far as to marry them! Once their true identity is discovered, however, they promptly leave, even if they've been together for years.<br /> <br /> <br /> The new version of handling Kiths and Seemings allows players to bring to life far more fairy tales and myths than the old version did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T06:32:49-07:00","id":493539,"title":"","content":"Oh wow your right David, there's beasts, elementals, fairest, Wizen, Orgers, Darklings. 100 x 6 is 600 combos. <br /> <br /> I'm really looking forward to this book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T06:51:24-07:00","id":493552,"title":"","content":"Since beasts no longer get 8 again on Animal Ken, a free animal specialization, and the ability to add dice to Compure and presence rolls, they only seem to get an ability to regain clarity ones per session, I'm guessing Kith Blessing must alot more powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T06:58:20-07:00","id":493559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=493062#post493062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yeah. We'll have sample Courts. But Court Creation is going to be a thing we encourage. I don't know how many individual Courts each sample city will have, so I can't tell you what kind of combination that'd make for yet.<br /> <br /> But the 500 estimate up there is off. Remember, six Seemings, 100 Kiths. So that's a base 600. <b>Even if you consider that some characters might not have a Seeming.</b><br /> <br /> REDACTED will give us another 100~ combinations. (And just to tease you all, REDACTED is actually Dark Eras. The Grimm's Fairy Tales Dark Era will have a new, Second Edition compliant Seeming.)<br /> <br /> If I get the chance to do my eighth Seeming, it'll add similarly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, there's a way to be without a seeming? That's an interesting possibility. Would that be like, someone who never managed to escape themselves, but was released by their keeper, or maybe rescued by someone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T07:47:21-07:00","id":493591,"title":"","content":"Or they're Keeper dies. Or they're a loyalist. or they find a way to escape that doesn't fit any seeming. Or maybe they're still in Arcadian, and they're escape is a manufactured lie mawhahaha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T07:49:36-07:00","id":493594,"title":"","content":"Custom Courts = More possibilities and fun times to be had!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T07:52:35-07:00","id":493597,"title":"","content":"No seeming is like the Seventh Seeming, Dark Eras Seeming is like the 8th, and the one in David's head is like the 9th. I'm assuming David's 9th seeming is Lovecraftian in nature and will slowly cause him to desend into madness, or it could be Princesses, which will cause to descend into madness far more quickly :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T09:20:20-07:00","id":493692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=493272#post493272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What Gaius said.<br /> <br /> Your Keeper abducts you, and turns you onto your Kith. Your Kith is the role you play in the Durance. When you escape, you flavour the Kith with a Seeming, based on how you took control and fled. So a Keeper might have needed a bunch of dragons. So, he abducts a bunch of Changelings and turns them into Draconic Kiths. But when the group decides to escape, they each choose a different method of escape. That means they're each still Draconic, but of different Seemings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for that clarification! I understand the setup much better now. It's good to see that being in Arcadia still matters and changes a fae. =)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T14:59:18-07:00","id":493968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=493559#post493559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, there's a way to be without a seeming? That's an interesting possibility. Would that be like, someone who never managed to escape themselves, but was released by their keeper, or maybe rescued by someone?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=493591#post493591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Or they're Keeper dies. Or they're a loyalist. or they find a way to escape that doesn't fit any seeming. Or maybe they're still in Arcadian, and they're escape is a manufactured lie mawhahaha.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> This brings up an interesting point: if any of these circumstances applies to your changeling, how does he develop a Seeming? I guess it would require him to take Agency in the mortal world, which has its own challenges and advantages.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T17:08:14-07:00","id":494077,"title":"","content":"Well since we're getting more Seemings in the future, methods that we think don't fit with any given Seeming now might actually fit with the new ones. So we'll have to wait and see. I'm curious as to what kind of other Seemings might exist, though, because the ones we have now seem to cover the basic fairy tail concepts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beast</b> - Animals both magical and mundane<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre</b> - powerful monsters such as trolls, giants and yetis<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened</b> - Wee Folk such as elves, gnomes and sprites<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest</b> - knights, princesses and other beloved characters<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling</b> - old wives tales, used to scare children into behaving.<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental</b> - spirits of the woodlands and other natural habitats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T17:24:43-07:00","id":494115,"title":"","content":"Well, the seventh Seeming is apparently appearing in a Dark Ages chapter, so we might need to consider the era they're going to show up in, like how the Lineage in the preview's Promethean chapter are so quintessentially Dust Bowl/Depression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T17:56:00-07:00","id":494142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=494115#post494115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the seventh Seeming is apparently appearing in a Dark Ages chapter, so we might need to consider the era they're going to show up in, like how the Lineage in the preview's Promethean chapter are so quintessentially Dust Bowl/Depression.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the Grimm's Fairy Tales era of Dark Eras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T18:24:00-07:00","id":494188,"title":"","content":"I have to wonder about these new Seemings. I'm sure it'll turn out awesome and I don't want to veer the topic off course, but I'm a guy that still likes picking a Seeming first and a Kith second.<br /> <br /> This is because I like that Seemings are sort of archetypes of different types of fairies or magical creatures. I think the six of them run the gamut of classical/typical depiction. So I wonder and hope that new Seemings won't be added just to represent different methods of escape, but that iconic fae types will be looked at first and then their theme of escape drawn from them secondly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T18:26:46-07:00","id":494192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=494188#post494188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to wonder about these new Seemings. I'm sure it'll turn out awesome and I don't want to veer the topic off course, but I'm a guy that still likes picking a Seeming first and a Kith second.<br /> <br /> This is because I like that Seemings are sort of archetypes of different types of fairies or magical creatures. I think the six of them run the gamut of classical/typical depiction. So I wonder and hope that new Seemings won't be added just to represent different methods of escape, but that iconic fae types will be looked at first and then their theme of escape drawn from them secondly</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a reason we're using the exact same six.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T19:48:50-07:00","id":494276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=494188#post494188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to wonder about these new Seemings. I'm sure it'll turn out awesome and I don't want to veer the topic off course, but I'm a guy that still likes picking a Seeming first and a Kith second.<br /> <br /> This is because I like that Seemings are sort of archetypes of different types of fairies or magical creatures. I think the six of them run the gamut of classical/typical depiction. So I wonder and hope that new Seemings won't be added just to represent different methods of escape, but that iconic fae types will be looked at first and then their theme of escape drawn from them secondly</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I for one love the new concept that any Kith can belong to any Seeming without having to Dual Kith to get it. While broad in options, the old method was still considered restrictive and made certain Fae interpretations impossible to bring to life. Also, Dual Kithing was expensive and caused players to sacrifice free points to make such a character. Now you can be anything you want and with 5(+) different ways to interpret the role!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Minstrel Beast</b> - A species of song bird?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Minstrel Elemental</b> - A Siren enchanting sailors near their reef?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Minstrel Ogre</b> - A skald or warrior poet?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Minstrel Darkling</b> - I'm not sure yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Minstrel Wizened</b> - hobbits, dwarves, gnomes?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Minstrel Fairest</b> - Tolkien Elves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-27-2015, 10:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T20:09:11-07:00","id":494287,"title":"","content":"I can see Darkling Minstrel's eating Nightsinger Kith the way Darkling Romancers ate the Succubi kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T20:11:45-07:00","id":494288,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't mind an example kith just to see how Kith/Seeming interact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T00:44:49-07:00","id":494499,"title":"","content":"There are so many kith already (92), though as talking to someone who wanted to play a mermaid before in a game, about four kith could cover that and there is little difference between them, outside of the Nix (the others being Swimmerskin, Waterborn and Waterdweller).<br /> I do like how Seeming coming after and exactly what it represents means that any Seeming picking these four kith can still be mermaids, though how they appear and act is what changes. Feels like players can make their character appear as what they want them to more freely now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T05:58:08-07:00","id":494672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=494499#post494499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are so many kith already (92), though as talking to someone who wanted to play a mermaid before in a game, about four kith could cover that and there is little difference between them, outside of the Nix (the others being Swimmerskin, Waterborn and Waterdweller).<br /> I do like how Seeming coming after and exactly what it represents means that any Seeming picking these four kith can still be mermaids, though how they appear and act is what changes. Feels like players can make their character appear as what they want them to more freely now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Which means some mermaids can be the beautiful singing type, and others can be the shark toothed cannibal type! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T06:10:27-07:00","id":494678,"title":"","content":"Okay, I'm not fully convinced to the new &quot;Kith leads to Seeming&quot; approach. As I read it now, I see you were Romancer under your Keeper, general &quot;beautiful people&quot;, elven like? But then you done things to escape and magically you can change in to: A) Succubi, if you choose Darkling way, B) Satyr, if you become animalistic, C) Truly elvish if you work like Fae and become Fairest?<br /> <br /> So you goes SECOND change after you run away from your Keeper? And True Fae do not change you in to more fantastic beings under your Durance? So the Horned Hunter do <b>not change</b> humans in to animals under his care? Doll Maker Fae do not change his humans in to dolls, only some plastic things? All his changelings are superficial &quot;nonhumans&quot;, without correct feel of their Mien?<br /> <br /> I can see as this way the game is more open, but from in-game perspective, character naratives is broken. It's like &quot;I'm highly specialized elvish courtesan, but I make myself grow goats horns and legs to run away and be better in what I do&quot; kinda thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T06:31:29-07:00","id":494699,"title":"","content":"As far as I understand, your Keeper does change you in any number of disturbing and fantastical ways; your Seeming is just you putting yourself through equally potent changes as a part of reclaiming your Agency. Like how the spoiler mentions Beasts whose Seeming animal and Kith animal clash tend to have decidedly Chimeric forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T06:32:53-07:00","id":494700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=494678#post494678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I'm not fully convinced to the new &amp;quot;Kith leads to Seeming&amp;quot; approach. As I read it now, I see you were Romancer under your Keeper, general &amp;quot;beautiful people&amp;quot;, elven like? But then you done things to escape and magically you can change in to: A) Succubi, if you choose Darkling way, B) Satyr, if you become animalistic, C) Truly elvish if you work like Fae and become Fairest?<br /> <br /> So you goes SECOND change after you run away from your Keeper? And True Fae do not change you in to more fantastic beings under your Durance? So the Horned Hunter do <b>not change</b> humans in to animals under his care? Doll Maker Fae do not change his humans in to dolls, only some plastic things? All his changelings are superficial &amp;quot;nonhumans&amp;quot;, without correct feel of their Mien?<br /> <br /> I can see as this way the game is more open, but from in-game perspective, character naratives is broken. It's like &amp;quot;I'm highly specialized elvish courtesan, but I make myself grow goats horns and legs to run away and be better in what I do&amp;quot; kinda thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, it's not a broken narrative, it's a changed narrative. <br /> <br /> Changelings are based are Wyrd, far magic, which as close as I can manage is tied to stories, dreams, and narratives. When the character breaks free, I'm not interpreting it as they are deciding to become beastial. Rather, the freeing of themselves and the breaking of the role the Keeper assigned to them is such a powerful change in the narrative dynamic that it changes the Wyrd within them. She doesn't choose to become a beast, she break free in a way that makes her Wyrd change her into a beast. Her Keeper took her by remaking her. She remakes herself to take her freedom back, and that leaves her a changed being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T06:44:32-07:00","id":494705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=494678#post494678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I'm not fully convinced to the new &quot;Kith leads to Seeming&quot; approach. As I read it now, I see you were Romancer under your Keeper, general &quot;beautiful people&quot;, elven like? But then you done things to escape and magically you can change in to: A) Succubi, if you choose Darkling way, B) Satyr, if you become animalistic, C) Truly elvish if you work like Fae and become Fairest?<br /> <br /> <b>1) </b>So you goes SECOND change after you run away from your Keeper? <b>2) </b>And True Fae do not change you in to more fantastic beings under your Durance? <b>3) </b>So the Horned Hunter do <b>not change</b> humans in to animals under his care? <b>4) </b>Doll Maker Fae do not change his humans in to dolls, only some plastic things? <b>5) </b>All his changelings are superficial &quot;nonhumans&quot;, without correct feel of their Mien?<br /> <br /> I can see as this way the game is more open, but from in-game perspective, character naratives is broken. It's like &quot;I'm highly specialized elvish courtesan, but I make myself grow goats horns and legs to run away and be better in what I do&quot; kinda thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>1)Yes, you do. Your character(henceforth referred to as you) takes the reigns of Arcadian power and changes who you are, what your place in the story is, and utterly escape under the power of your newly self-written narrative.<br /> <br /> Yes, this means changelings escaping Durance became <i>even more badass</i>.<br /> <br /> 2) This is a poor reading. THere are probably kiths for herd animals and trees and dolls. But reclaiming yourself means not taking that shit, and while you will be scarred with your kith for the rest of your life, you can become...well, not human again, but humanoid.<br /> <br /> 3) This is a poor reading.<br /> <br /> 4) This is a poor reading.<br /> <br /> 5) Look, if I'm blunt, I don't see why you would ever think that**. (Read as: This is a poor reading.)<br /> <br /> It reflects CHOICE. It reflects AGECNY.<br /> <br /> And it does this in a world where CHOICE is inherently tied to CHANGE, where narrative <i>is</i> physicality, where plot twists <i>change the world</i>.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you expected to happen. This is a world where Prankster's Paradise from Pinocchio* makes sense, as an example.<br /> <br /> *In the movie at least, the more you make an ass of yourself in this place, the more you turn into a donkey, ie, an ass, in case it's not common knowledge for everyone.<br /> <br /> **I want to expand on this a little. In First Edition, your Kith was the result of your basic structure being warped and twisted by the Stranger, and your seeming was how that Kith tapped into a larger archetypal mass and drew power from it. THey were closely knit together. So, after that happened, you went until you came to the soundness of mind and the strength of your cojones(shut up, it makes sense in my head), at which point you escape, and in doing so...reclaimed a physical human form that could warp and devolve on the way down? I make a question mark there, but it's really for the same reason-in escaping, you reclaimed your humanity*** and forced a human shape on yourself with Arcadian powers.<br /> <br /> This style and approach to the physicality of a changeling has always been there, it just hasn't always been explained very well. Second Edition now makes it clear what's going on.<br /> <br /> ***Which is another reason I kept getting annoyed at the &quot;Elementals sacrifice humanity to leave&quot; reading from the earlier thread. The sacrificed humanity thing always made more sense when the Strangers ripped too much out. Still, we'll see if Dave disagrees with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-28-2015, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T07:10:59-07:00","id":494753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=494678#post494678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I'm not fully convinced to the new &quot;Kith leads to Seeming&quot; approach. As I read it now, I see you were Romancer under your Keeper, general &quot;beautiful people&quot;, elven like? But then you done things to escape and magically you can change in to: A) Succubi, if you choose Darkling way, B) Satyr, if you become animalistic, C) Truly elvish if you work like Fae and become Fairest?<br /> <br /> So you goes SECOND change after you run away from your Keeper? And True Fae do not change you in to more fantastic beings under your Durance? So the Horned Hunter do <b>not change</b> humans in to animals under his care? Doll Maker Fae do not change his humans in to dolls, only some plastic things? All his changelings are superficial &quot;nonhumans&quot;, without correct feel of their Mien?<br /> <br /> I can see as this way the game is more open, but from in-game perspective, character naratives is broken. It's like &quot;I'm highly specialized elvish courtesan, but I make myself grow goats horns and legs to run away and be better in what I do&quot; kinda thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There are many different legends regarding Fae and monsters than what is portrayed in the past version. I believe the Keeper would turn you into an animal or something, but depending on your Seeming affects how that animal is portrayed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Take for example, a Keeper who wants a pet wolf. A Changeling who becomes a Beast might simply take on the characteristics of a wolf upon their escape. But an Ogre might become something closer to a Dire Wolf or possibly even a Worg (demonic wolves, pretty much). A Fairest who gets turned into a wolf might have a beautiful, shiny coat and be a majestic creature of the forest. Darklings might be predatory hunters or turned into pseudo-lycanthropes. Wizened might be used to perform various tasks such as pulling a sleigh or hunting game. Elementals, I'm not sure of just yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> So to reiterate; yes, your keeper may turn into an animal or a doll or whatever, but your Seeming has some impact on how that transformation manifests itself. It sounds like it offers a lot more freedom and customization than the old &quot;here's a list of options, pick one.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Remember that your Kith is the job you were given, and your Seeming is how you took control of your life again. As for the courtesan growing goat horns, maybe they resort to headbutting the guards in order to make an escape? So the courtesan sang, danced and drank, pretty much being a good party planner. Then one day they decide to escape and headbutt one of their guards into submission, stealing their keys and making a run for it! On the way out, they keep bowling through anyone who tries to stop them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-28-2015, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T07:55:11-07:00","id":494796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=494753#post494753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take for example, a Keeper who wants a pet wolf. A Changeling who becomes a Beast might simply take on the characteristics of a wolf upon their escape. But an Ogre might become something closer to a Dire Wolf or possibly even a Worg (demonic wolves, pretty much). A Fairest who gets turned into a wolf might have a beautiful, shiny coat and be a majestic creature of the forest. Darklings might be predatory hunters or turned into pseudo-lycanthropes. Wizened might be used to perform various tasks such as pulling a sleigh or hunting game. Elementals, I'm not sure of just yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadow Elemental Wolf.<br /> <br /> Who's afraid of the Big Bad Wolf?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T08:27:15-07:00","id":494854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=494678#post494678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you goes SECOND change after you run away from your Keeper?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup.<br /> <br /> It's <i>textual</i>, so I'm not sure where the point of confusion is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prologue: The Icicle Melts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We remember what it\u2019s like to be trapped someplace where the possibility of escape doesn\u2019t exist. At least, until something changes.<br /> <br /> Something changes. Ha. To escape Arcadia, <u>you</u> have to change. You have to let it into you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=494796#post494796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shadow Elemental Wolf.<br /> <br /> Who's afraid of the Big Bad Wolf?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;Oh, but you must travel through those woods again and again\u2026&quot; <a href=\"http://wonsab.tumblr.com/post/117313897270/alkthash-emily-carroll-this-fucked-me-up-guys\" target=\"_blank\">said a shadow at the window</a>.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-28-2015, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T08:34:37-07:00","id":494858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=494753#post494753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take for example, a Keeper who wants a pet wolf. A Changeling who becomes a Beast might simply take on the characteristics of a wolf upon their escape. But an Ogre might become something closer to a Dire Wolf or possibly even a Worg (demonic wolves, pretty much). A Fairest who gets turned into a wolf might have a beautiful, shiny coat and be a majestic creature of the forest. Darklings might be predatory hunters or turned into pseudo-lycanthropes. Wizened might be used to perform various tasks such as pulling a sleigh or hunting game. Elementals, I'm not sure of just yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part about the &quot;transformation in details&quot; I get - the outlook change. I do not get <b>logic</b> of it. HOW becoming more like animal your Keeper wanted you to be, can help you to free for him? You make <b>exactly</b> what he wanted to do you into first place. HOW becoming beautyfull wolf can free you? Even becoming Shadow Wolf. You are still A WOLF the Keeper wanted you to be, don't you?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=494753#post494753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So to reiterate; yes, your keeper may turn into an animal or a doll or whatever, but your Seeming has some impact on how that transformation manifests itself. It sounds like it offers a lot more freedom and customization than the old &quot;here's a list of options, pick one.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not argue that this way game is much more open. Only the result narrative is <b>really</b> strange one. Like mine &quot;courtesan in to Beast&quot; example.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=494753#post494753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that your Kith is the job you were given, and your Seeming is how you took control of your life again. As for the courtesan growing goat horns, maybe they resort to headbutting the guards in order to make an escape? So the courtesan sang, danced and drank, pretty much being a good party planner. Then one day they decide to escape and headbutt one of their guards into submission, stealing their keys and making a run for it! On the way out, they keep bowling through anyone who tries to stop them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'm weird one ( or WYRD one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) but I would rather see developing your Seeming as something much more profound than &quot;I headbutt one guardsman on the run&quot;. I could somehow go the way of corteasan becoming &quot;sexual beast&quot;, going in to sex rampage with all the gurads in the Keepers palace to make them all dependent on her and she being freed from her job as being dedicated only to her Keeper as lover. Still, it's seems so strange story like this...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-28-2015, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T08:35:51-07:00","id":494859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=494854#post494854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>&quot;Oh, but you must travel through those woods again and again\u2026&quot; <a href=\"http://wonsab.tumblr.com/post/117313897270/alkthash-emily-carroll-this-fucked-me-up-guys\" target=\"_blank\">said a shadow at the window</a>.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>This has made my day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:03:21-07:00","id":494885,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that your kith encompasses your job in its entirety. You're still able to be a wolfperson or a tree or a gravedigger or whatever. The Seeming just colors that. So now your wolfperson is shadowy and weird or your grave digger might just be really feral and not necessarily have horns or hooves or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:13:07-07:00","id":494894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=494858#post494858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part about the &quot;transformation in details&quot; I get - the outlook change. I do not get <b>logic</b> of it. HOW becoming more like animal your Keeper wanted you to be, can help you to free for him? You make <b>exactly</b> what he wanted to do you into first place. HOW becoming beautyfull wolf can free you? Even becoming Shadow Wolf. You are still A WOLF the Keeper wanted you to be, don't you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Seeming is about your escape. It's not about what the Others wanted you to do, or how they planned it. It's about how <i>you set yourself free and how that redefines you by your own standards</i>. Your Keeper turned you into a hunting animal in Arcadia. When you ran, you didn't resist it - you used that beastial nature to evade the Huntsmen. In doing so, you made your kith <i>yours</i>, by taking control of the narrative that was forced on you. It doesn't matter if your Keeper wanted to reduce you to a beast to begin with. This change, the shaping that is your Seeming, came from your agency. So even if it somehow invokes what your abuser did or intended, it is something <i>you own, not them</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 04-28-2015, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:17:11-07:00","id":494926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=494858#post494858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Part about the &quot;transformation in details&quot; I get - the outlook change. I do not get <b>logic</b> of it. HOW becoming more like animal your Keeper wanted you to be, can help you to free for him? You make <b>exactly</b> what he wanted to do you into first place. HOW becoming beautyfull wolf can free you? Even becoming Shadow Wolf. You are still A WOLF the Keeper wanted you to be, don't you?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You're still a wolf, but your are not anymore HIS wolf. The Gentry took you and shape you according to their whims through the Wyrd. But the only way to escape is to understand the Wyrd yourself and use a narrative way to flee. Fleeing by indulging your instinct, fleeing by revolting, fleeing by stoping caring about anything. And if you use the Wyrd, the Wyrd use you, and you fall further away from humanity.<br /> <br /> Your keeper can change you into animal or a doll, what you become after is up to you. For the doll :<br /> - Beast doll : plushies (Pooh with fang !)<br /> - Darkling doll : Chucky !<br /> - Elemental doll : Pinocchio<br /> - Ogre doll : patchwork like Frankestein' monster<br /> - Fairest doll : a delicate automaton which danse in a music box<br /> - Wizened doll : a clockwork-style mechanical tool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3883-arabidopsis","name":"Arabidopsis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:40:10-07:00","id":494948,"title":"","content":"The actual fluff of the escape is up to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:46:55-07:00","id":494955,"title":"","content":"<b>@wyrdhamster:</b> Your Keeper took you and changed you; they <i>made</i> you into that Courtesan. It's you, but it's not <i>really</i> you. Plus, the whole <i>world</i> is arranged so that none of the options open to you as a Courtesan will get you out. The story in play is &quot;How The Keeper Took a Mortal Man as Bride&quot;; it's got the force of the Wyrd behind it, and creatures of narrative can't <i>break</i> that. That story might as well be the laws of physics; heck, in Arcadia, it's <i>stronger.</i><br /> <br /> Good thing you aren't a creature of narrative; you are a son of mankind, and as soon as you remember that, you can leave. Because one of our greatest strengths is that we're <i>storytellers</i> - and your escape is a better story than whatever derivative trash your Keeper had you doing. Once you've started, the <i>only</i> beings that can stop your escape are other <i>people</i> (and Keepers aren't people); you've got the force of the Wyrd behind you, and creature's of narrative can't <i>stop</i> that.<br /> <br /> But the laws of the Wyrd are a harsh mistress - while no one can stop you, <i>you can't escape as you are</i>. If you're the Hero, you can't reclaim your home without becoming a stranger to it; your stay in Arcadia <i>must</i> leave you changed. And the impositions of your Keeper don't - <i>can't</i> - count; they're the thing chaining you to the story you were forced into. So all that's left is to change yourself through your exit-arc.<br /> <br /> <i>Once upon a time, there was a satyr trapped in a sumptuous palace; they thought he was tamed, a pretty toy for love and romance. But one fateful night...</i><br /> <i>Once there was a dainty maiden, a virgin demure, trapped in a tower with a single door. This door would only open for those with carnal knowledge - &quot;Is that all it takes?&quot; - and the virgin was a virgin no more...</i><br /> <i>Once there was a handsome young man who was promised to a great and terrible lord and who was forbidden to leave his tor by great and terrible laws. So he courted and seduced that great lord, bringing a smile to his face and warmth to his heart. &quot;Tell me, my love; tell me what you wish, and I'll give it to you!&quot; &quot;Oh great prince, there is only one thing I wish...&quot;</i><br /> <br /> And so on and so forth.<br /> <hr /><br /> As I wrote the above, I got to thinking... since Arcadia runs on Gentry Logic, wouldn't redefining your story by gaining a Seeming retroactively affect your Durance? Or, rather, you always had both your Kith and your Seeming, because your escape changed the story of your Durance so that the Seeming was always there. An abstraction of the process would be that the Durance is your <i>Keeper</i> telling the story of your stay in Arcadia, while your escape is you retelling the story in such an awesome way that the Keeper just kinda blinks and then goes &quot;Oh, yes, exactly like the story I just told. What? It wasn't? You must have misheard me; that was <i>clearly</i> the same as the story I just told.&quot;<br /> <br /> Because Keepers are the <i>biggest</i> plagiarists, and you just told a better version. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BGi6Q1pNbS0\" target=\"_blank\">With blackjack. And hookers*.</a><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*The blackjack and hookers might just be for Ogres - we'll have to wait and see.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:53:18-07:00","id":494966,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Thanks, <b>amechra</b>, you sum up what I was trying to understand nicely. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arabidopsis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=494926#post494926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're still a wolf, but your are not anymore HIS wolf. The Gentry took you and shape you according to their whims through the Wyrd. But the only way to escape is to understand the Wyrd yourself and use a narrative way to flee. Fleeing by indulging your instinct, fleeing by revolting, fleeing by stoping caring about anything. And if you use the Wyrd, the Wyrd use you, and you fall further away from humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>You see, now I get it. In text, there is not any conottion of the Wyrd tranforming you. On first reading it was &quot;you were soposed to be wolf by yur Keeper - puff - you are shadow wolf now&quot;. I could et get the wrap of my head tht the running away from your Keeper would change you - it was True Fae that made you in to you Kith. But if Seemings are streaming from Wyrd - and it's a bit like &quot;and so you are blessed/curessed with hooves by Wyrd for breaking the Contracts your Keepers put on you&quot; - now it is much more logical narrative. The Wyrd is &quot;punishing&quot; ( maybe &quot;marking&quot; is better word here? ) PCs from breaking away the relations Keeper placed on you in Arcadia. In this light, yes, Seeming IS <b>a scar</b> of some sort. And everything has - at least - fairy tale logic to it now for me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, to sum up, here is now mortal-to-changeling process:<br /> <br /> 1. Mortal is kidnaped by True Fae.<br /> 2. His Keeper place a Kith on him in Arcadia by &quot;fullfiling his role&quot;.<br /> 3. Changeling is running away, breaking the promise Fae put on his life role ( the Kith. in reality ).<br /> 4. Wyrd is &quot;marking&quot; character with Seeming, showing the signs of the way he broke the Keepers promise to the Wyrd.<br /> <br /> I get it right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-28-2015, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T11:00:41-07:00","id":495017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=494966#post494966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get it right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's it. A Changeling could certainly see the marks of both Kith and Seeming as scars, but that's not exactly the default (well, for Kith, perhaps). Breaking a contract isn't the thing.<br /> <br /> You are dancing in the right ballroom with fairy tale logic, though. Try this. The character had his story defined for him, when he was taken and twisted into his Kith. Whether it was the Gentry or Arcadia itself that did it, he was suddenly playing a scripted story not of his own devising and thus was his agency taken. As a consequence, taking back that agency, declaring through his actions before the Wyrd and the world that this story is <i>his</i> and it will become what <i>he</i> makes of it is an incredibly powerful thing. The Wyrd can't help but respond.<br /> <br /> It's not that headbutting someone makes him a Beast, it's what the headbutt <i>means</i>. It's that he snarls that he will not be chained, and lets no long-ingrained notions of civilized behavior hold him back from breaking free. The Wyrd finds this wild abandon resonant with that of a Beast, and so a Beast he becomes -- and makes of himself -- in his act of will. Should the powerful act of taking back his life have a different form with a different resonance, then that different resonance is what his will and the Wyrd will fold into the story of the life his action is writing. That defines his Seeming.<br /> <br /> If anything, it would be closer to think <i>not</i> of him being punished for breaking a contract, and instead of forging and negotiating a new contract with the Wyrd. Or, in an abstract sense, having his agency taken is like being part of a contract that reads, &quot;I will always be a &lt;Kith&gt;,&quot; and then taking that agency back is like finding a loophole to exploit: &quot;I will always be a &lt;Kith&gt;, but here is what I've decided that will actually <i>mean</i>.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T11:06:19-07:00","id":495026,"title":"","content":"If the Seeming's a scar, it's from ripping the plot hooks out of your skin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T13:28:50-07:00","id":495128,"title":"","content":"The Seeming is absolutely a scar. That doesn't mean it can't eventually become a badge of honor like other scars can, but its the literal manifestation of you seizing your agency and liberating yourself. Just because you've taken charge of the situation doesn't mean the situation is any less horrible. Fear is still fear, violence is still violence, and the weight of that doesn't disappear just because you're in the right. &quot;Doing what it takes to survive&quot; is almost always traumatic as all hell. PTSD does<i> not</i> care if you were holding the steering wheel or if your cause was just.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T13:54:22-07:00","id":495160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. Mortal is kidnaped by True Fae.<br /> 2. His Keeper place a Kith on him in Arcadia by &quot;fullfiling his role&quot;. </div> </div> </div>It's more like the Keeper assigns them a role and that role is the Kith. They want your mortal character to be their toy puppet. Suddenly they find themselves as a doll on strings by fae magick for the Keeper's amusement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Changeling is running away, breaking the promise Fae put on his life role ( the Kith. in reality ).<br /> 4. Wyrd is &quot;marking&quot; character with Seeming, showing the signs of the way he broke the Keepers promise to the Wyrd. </div> </div> </div>The Kith stays with the character, at least the markings of it. Whilst their escape from Arcadia means that is not who they are anymore, they still hold the physical and mental scarring of that time. The puppet man from above is still the man made of wood, however by <b><i>proactively</i></b> letting go of the last of their humanity in escaping, by letting the animal within them rush them kicking and screaming back through the Hedge and into reality, they gain their Seeming of the Beast and now they look more like a beastial marionette than a human one.<br /> <br /> At least that's how I've read how it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T14:08:41-07:00","id":495179,"title":"","content":"The way I look at it you can't remove your kith, its replaced key parts of you body and soul with glamour, but you can shape it, the way an athetlete shapes they're body, only instead of exercise you do it will your escape, which changes you, both physically, spiritually, mentally, and mystically, this is your seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T14:31:48-07:00","id":495224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=494894#post494894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your Seeming is about your escape. It's not about what the Others wanted you to do, or how they planned it. It's about how <i>you set yourself free and how that redefines you by your own standards</i>. Your Keeper turned you into a hunting animal in Arcadia. When you ran, you didn't resist it - you used that beastial nature to evade the Huntsmen. In doing so, you made your kith <i>yours</i>, by taking control of the narrative that was forced on you. It doesn't matter if your Keeper wanted to reduce you to a beast to begin with. This change, the shaping that is your Seeming, came from your agency. So even if it somehow invokes what your abuser did or intended, it is something <i>you own, not them</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's like at the end of Ghost Rider when he's offered the chance to become human. Instead he says that he's going to take his curse and use it against the devil. In that moment, Johnny Blaze became a Darkling... or maybe an Elemental. hard to tell with a flaming skeleton who only roams at night.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for how a doll might escape, I imagine that as an elemental, you play the Toy Story route. When your Keeper enters the room, you become a cold, lifeless object. Nothing the Keeper does (including placing you in physical harm) elicits any kind of reaction out of you. Your Keeper grows bored and decides to throw you out with the trash, and that's when you spring your escape!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-28-2015, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T15:57:20-07:00","id":495338,"title":"","content":"I kinda hope the dual merits are still a thing cause I'd like to do up an Elemental Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T16:41:48-07:00","id":495385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanandithras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=495338#post495338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda hope the dual merits are still a thing cause I'd like to do up an Elemental Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time will tell if and how they decide to go for something like Dual Kith (I don't remember a Dual Seeming Merit; did I miss that one?). I could see a case for it not being necessary in 2e: it kind of already works in the baseline system. If one wants to make a character with both animal and elemental traits, one can choose/fluff a Kith with animal traits and take the Elemental Seeming or choose/fluff a Kith with elemental traits and take the Beast Seeming. Which one you take would depend on what you want to emphasize.<br /> <br /> I'd certainly dig seeing Dual Kith again, though. In the new context, Kiths seem to provide more of the innate fey talents/capabilities of the Changeling, while Seemings' metaphysical oomph (Clarity aside*) comes from Contract affinities. It'd be nice to have the option of a Seeming sometimes manifesting a second Kith through that Merit; if a Minstrel becomes a leonine Beast, it'd be neat for an extra Kith to reflect the claws and fangs or what have you.<br /> <br /> * Also aside anything else we may not know about. &gt;.&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T17:40:35-07:00","id":495483,"title":"","content":"Maybe Dual Kiths are the result of Keepers getting bored with your role and changing you into something else more suited to their tastes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T18:03:27-07:00","id":495507,"title":"","content":"I want to feel out Kiths before I introduce Dual Kith. I don't want to make something that feels superfluous or clunky. If it happens, it'll happen in second draft territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T18:03:48-07:00","id":495509,"title":"","content":"My only worry about Dual Kiths from what we know so far, is that Kith bonuses are supposed to be a lot more potent; replacing the minor Kith bonuses and Seeming bonuses in value is my impression.<br /> <br /> That means Dual Kith, from a balance perspective, is suddenly a lot more powerful. A lot of Kith bonuses could be approximated with 2-3 dot Merits in 1e without Dual Kith; but it doesn't sound like that will holdover as well in 2e.<br /> <br /> I think, rather than Dual Kith, I'd rather see a more customizable Wyrd Evolution system. Combined with the intended customizable Courts, it seems like you'd cover a lot more thematic ground that way. And we still have Entitlements to add more customization with as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T18:07:57-07:00","id":495517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=495509#post495509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only worry about Dual Kiths from what we know so far, is that Kith bonuses are supposed to be a lot more potent; replacing the minor Kith bonuses and Seeming bonuses in value is my impression.<br /> <br /> That means Dual Kith, from a balance perspective, is suddenly a lot more powerful. A lot of Kith bonuses could be approximated with 2-3 dot Merits in 1e without Dual Kith; but it doesn't sound like that will holdover as well in 2e.<br /> <br /> I think, rather than Dual Kith, I'd rather see a more customizable Wyrd Evolution system. Combined with the intended customizable Courts, it seems like you'd cover a lot more thematic ground that way. And we still have Entitlements to add more customization with as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most definitely. <br /> <br /> I think we'll be able to have more distinct discussion about potential Dual Kith stuff once I post Kiths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T18:12:40-07:00","id":495523,"title":"","content":"I don't mind seeing Dual-Kiths in a supplement rather than the corebook tough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T18:17:56-07:00","id":495527,"title":"","content":"The way the Kiths work now is so awesome. They're a lot of fun. SO MUCH FUN. I'll bet you all wish you could read it, couldn't you? Mwahahaha!<br /> <br /> Oh, don't worry. You'll get to see them. And I, too, want to see some Dual Kiths or Wyrd evolution come into play. I like playing my Fireheart/Windwing Spring phoenix concept, and there are lots of other combinations I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> And yes, the new Kith bonuses rock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Claire C. \u2022 <b>Gaea Games Developer </b>\u2022 <b>Onyx Path Freelancer</b> (a.k.a. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield\" target=\"_blank\">Claire Redfield</a>)<br /> Now on Kickstarter: <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/1027237145/city-of-the-dead\" target=\"_blank\"><b>City of the Dead</b></a>, my survival horror roleplaying game introducing the GAEA System. COTD includes special emphasis on building and rebuilding communities, mental and social abilitiies.<br /> Twitter: <a href=\"https://twitter.com/GaeaGames\" target=\"_blank\">@GaeaGames</a> \u2022 Patreon: <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/GaeaGames\" target=\"_blank\">GaeaGames</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5822-gaea-games","name":"Gaea Games","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5822_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T18:34:32-07:00","id":495582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaea Games</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=495527#post495527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way the Kiths work now is so awesome. They're a lot of fun. SO MUCH FUN. I'll bet you all wish you could read it, couldn't you? Mwahahaha!<br /> <br /> Oh, don't worry. You'll get to see them. And I, too, want to see some Dual Kiths or Wyrd evolution come into play. I like playing my Fireheart/Windwing Spring phoenix concept, and there are lots of other combinations I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> And yes, the new Kith bonuses rock.</div> </div> </div> </div>Joke's on you. <br /> <br /> I just posted them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths/\" target=\"_blank\"> Changeling the Lost Second Edition: Kiths &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T19:05:51-07:00","id":495617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=495582#post495582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Joke's on you.<br /> <br /> I just posted them.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-th...edition-kiths/</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Question:</b> What if we don't like having God Machine in our games? In my personal setting, the GM doesn't exist and all references to it are thrown out. How will that affect Kiths being used in the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T19:08:10-07:00","id":495622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=495617#post495617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Question:</b> What if we don't like having God Machine in our games? In my personal setting, the GM doesn't exist and all references to it are thrown out. How will that affect Kiths being used in the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kiths don't in any way relate to the God-Machine. Changeling the Lost won't reference the God-Machine, outside maybe an oblique seed or something. <br /> <br /> If you're talking about the page references, those are just references to Merits. Those will be in the final draft version of Lost; they're just in there so I know to put them in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T19:40:53-07:00","id":495654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=495582#post495582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Joke's on you.<br /> <br /> I just posted them.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-th...edition-kiths/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Curse you, HIIIIIIIIIIILLLLLLL!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Claire C. \u2022 <b>Gaea Games Developer </b>\u2022 <b>Onyx Path Freelancer</b> (a.k.a. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield\" target=\"_blank\">Claire Redfield</a>)<br /> Now on Kickstarter: <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/1027237145/city-of-the-dead\" target=\"_blank\"><b>City of the Dead</b></a>, my survival horror roleplaying game introducing the GAEA System. COTD includes special emphasis on building and rebuilding communities, mental and social abilitiies.<br /> Twitter: <a href=\"https://twitter.com/GaeaGames\" target=\"_blank\">@GaeaGames</a> \u2022 Patreon: <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/GaeaGames\" target=\"_blank\">GaeaGames</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5822-gaea-games","name":"Gaea Games","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5822_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T20:38:09-07:00","id":495740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaea Games</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=495654#post495654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curse you, HIIIIIIIIIIILLLLLLL!!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, look on the bright side: you got in significantly more gloating than the other freelancers, and David can't take that away from you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T21:03:19-07:00","id":495853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=495622#post495622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kiths don't in any way relate to the God-Machine. Changeling the Lost won't reference the God-Machine, outside maybe an oblique seed or something.<br /> <br /> If you're talking about the page references, those are just references to Merits. Those will be in the final draft version of Lost; they're just in there so I know to put them in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ah, thanks for clarifying that! :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T22:03:13-07:00","id":495895,"title":"","content":"Correct me if I'm wrong, but you seem to have specifically focused on Seemings that fall outside the norm when giving examples of each Kith.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing this is to provide less obvious methods to envision them for those who need some ideas? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T22:17:30-07:00","id":495916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=495740#post495740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, look on the bright side: you got in significantly more gloating than the other freelancers, and David can't take that away from you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's the whole reason I tried so hard to get into this industry. Not to create enjoyable games. Not to make my mark on the hobby I've enjoyed since single-digit youth. Simply to gloat over the other fans when I know something they don't. And now...my master stroke is come to fruition, and I reap the mild envy of my peers like the ambrosia to sustain my immortal glee! HAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAAAA!<br /> <br /> ... hm. I need to do some more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Claire C. \u2022 <b>Gaea Games Developer </b>\u2022 <b>Onyx Path Freelancer</b> (a.k.a. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield\" target=\"_blank\">Claire Redfield</a>)<br /> Now on Kickstarter: <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/1027237145/city-of-the-dead\" target=\"_blank\"><b>City of the Dead</b></a>, my survival horror roleplaying game introducing the GAEA System. COTD includes special emphasis on building and rebuilding communities, mental and social abilitiies.<br /> Twitter: <a href=\"https://twitter.com/GaeaGames\" target=\"_blank\">@GaeaGames</a> \u2022 Patreon: <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/GaeaGames\" target=\"_blank\">GaeaGames</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5822-gaea-games","name":"Gaea Games","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5822_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T22:27:38-07:00","id":495930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=495895#post495895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I'm wrong, but you seem to have specifically focused on Seemings that fall outside the norm when giving examples of each Kith.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing this is to provide less obvious methods to envision them for those who need some ideas? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I felt that some were so obvious so as to be wasting words. This philosophy saved us a lot of space, and gave us room to deliver more story hooks. Which is pretty much my biggest thing when developing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T22:50:01-07:00","id":495940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaea Games</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=495916#post495916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the whole reason I tried so hard to get into this industry. Not to create enjoyable games. Not to make my mark on the hobby I've enjoyed since single-digit youth. Simply to gloat over the other fans when I know something they don't. And now...my master stroke is come to fruition, and I reap the mild envy of my peers like the ambrosia to sustain my immortal glee! HAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAAAA!<br /> <br /> ... hm. I need to do some more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can respect this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Kudos to you!<br /> <br /> One tried and tested method I've seen involves issuing a description of stuff that has you psyched, but peppering it with enough [REDACTED]s that David doesn't mind it going out, and then watching in amusement as people flail about trying to decipher it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T22:56:16-07:00","id":495944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=495940#post495940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can respect this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Kudos to you!<br /> <br /> One tried and tested method I've seen involves issuing a description of stuff that has you psyched, but peppering it with enough [REDACTED]s that David doesn't mind it going out, and then watching in amusement as people flail about trying to decipher it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] [REDACTED] idea. [REDACTED] should be [REDACTED] soon.<br /> <br /> ____<br /> <br /> Now with the kiths stuff released, this makes this section more exciting. I've got a few PCs in my game, that I'd like to see dressed up as 2E characters. Could be awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T02:21:35-07:00","id":496108,"title":"","content":"After reading the example Kiths, I'm even less convinced that Dual Kiths should return.<br /> <br /> With most Kiths having multiple powers, and the text being very encouraging of tweaking things to fit your vision of the character, the thematic drive behind the Dual Kith Merit seems replaced by simply mixing Kiths together to make a new one. If you wanted to do a Fireheart/Windwing, you don't need a Merit any more. Just to work with your ST to, say, take the extended action bonus from Fireheart and replace it with a flight/glide power. Remixing the 2e Kiths is far easier than the 1e Kiths, and avoids trying to figure out what a Dual Kith Merit should cost.<br /> <br /> Though I'm even more excited about speculating on Wyrd Evolution in 2e with the greater focus on flexibility and customization the game seems to be taking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T02:45:25-07:00","id":496110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=496108#post496108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading the example Kiths, I'm even less convinced that Dual Kiths should return.<br /> <br /> With most Kiths having multiple powers, and the text being very encouraging of tweaking things to fit your vision of the character, the thematic drive behind the Dual Kith Merit seems replaced by simply mixing Kiths together to make a new one. If you wanted to do a Fireheart/Windwing, you don't need a Merit any more. Just to work with your ST to, say, take the extended action bonus from Fireheart and replace it with a flight/glide power. Remixing the 2e Kiths is far easier than the 1e Kiths, and avoids trying to figure out what a Dual Kith Merit should cost.<br /> <br /> Though I'm even more excited about speculating on Wyrd Evolution in 2e with the greater focus on flexibility and customization the game seems to be taking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure this is the stance we'll be taking in this book. I'm still listening for other commentary. But so far, I think they're not too necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T05:07:47-07:00","id":496187,"title":"","content":"I agree, the new Blessings seem to be a huge improvement over the originals. I hope that the Oni aren't restricted to using Mouthful of Sin once per session, this time around, as that always struck me as kind of odd since all it did was heal their wounds and could only be used on evil people. Seeing the overhaul the Leech Fingers received (can heal massive amounts of health with enough Glamour), it looks like they might get a power up too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-29-2015, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T09:31:46-07:00","id":496374,"title":"","content":"So reading the Kith stuff got my creative juices flowing, and realizing. A great &quot;Dark Era&quot; for Changeling?<br /> <br /> Heian Japan.<br /> <br /> Realize it's probably too late right now for the current one. But in the future, it could be fascinating. A very artistic culture in the core. Very 'civil society' - while out on the fringes are war and other things.<br /> <br /> Mostly though, it was the writeup for Telluric and staring at the stars that made me think it. A person out 'gazing at the moon' being taken for whatever reason. Or an Artist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T14:12:38-07:00","id":496747,"title":"","content":"I can agree with the idea of a Yokai / Hanyou Seeming... or would that fall under the category of Kith? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-29-2015, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T14:16:23-07:00","id":496749,"title":"","content":"Yokai would be seeming, but I'm fairly sure that cultural distinctiveness does not a point of agency make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T14:19:56-07:00","id":496752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=496749#post496749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yokai would be seeming, but I'm fairly sure that cultural distinctiveness does not a point of agency make.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hmm, after first going through the Wiki, I was thinking they sounded like a Kith, but another look through showed they have a wide number of capabilities, so a Seeming does seem appropriate.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------<br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><b>Y\u014dkai</b></i> (\u5996\u602a<sup><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Installing_Japanese_character_sets\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000EE\"><b>?</b></span></a></sup>, <i><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghost\" target=\"_blank\">ghost</a></i>, <i>phantom</i>, <i>strange apparition</i>) are a class of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supernatural\" target=\"_blank\">supernatural</a> monsters in <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_folklore\" target=\"_blank\">Japanese folklore</a>. The word y\u014dkai is made up of the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kanji\" target=\"_blank\">kanji</a> for &quot;bewitching; attractive; calamity&quot; and &quot;apparition; mystery; suspicious&quot;.<sup><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Y%C5%8Dkai#cite_note-1\" target=\"_blank\">[1]</a></sup> They can also be called <b>ayakashi</b> (\u5996<sup><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Installing_Japanese_character_sets\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000EE\"><b>?</b></span></a></sup>), <b><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mononoke\" target=\"_blank\">mononoke</a></b> (\u7269\u306e\u602a<sup><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Installing_Japanese_character_sets\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000EE\"><b>?</b></span></a></sup>), or <b>mamono</b> (\u9b54\u7269<sup><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Installing_Japanese_character_sets\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000EE\"><b>?</b></span></a></sup>). Y\u014dkai range eclectically from the malevolent to the mischievous, or occasionally bring good fortune to those who encounter them. Often they possess animal features (such as the <i><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kappa_(folklore)\" target=\"_blank\">Kappa</a></i>, which is similar to a turtle, or the <i><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tengu\" target=\"_blank\">Tengu</a></i> which has wings), other times they can appear mostly human, some look like inanimate objects and others have no discernible shape. <i>Y\u014dkai</i> usually have a spiritual supernatural power, with <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shapeshifting\" target=\"_blank\">shapeshifting</a> being one of the most common. <i>Y\u014dkai</i> that have the ability to shapeshift are called <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Obake\" target=\"_blank\">obake</a>.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Japanese folklorists and historians use <i>y\u014dkai</i> as &quot;supernatural or unaccountable phenomena to their informants&quot;. In the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edo_period\" target=\"_blank\">Edo period</a>, many artists, such as <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toriyama_Sekien\" target=\"_blank\">Toriyama Sekien</a>, created <i>y\u014dkai</i> inspired by folklore or their own ideas, and in the present, several <i>y\u014dkai</i> created by them (e.g. Kameosa and <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amikiri\" target=\"_blank\">Amikiri</a>, see below) are wrongly considered as being of legendary origin.<sup><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Y%C5%8Dkai#cite_note-2\" target=\"_blank\">[2]</a></sup></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-29-2015, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T14:26:20-07:00","id":496778,"title":"","content":"I'm not a hundred percent sure how a wide selection of various spirit/fairy/monsters counts as a Kith, but then again I'm having trouble doing anything other than swapping the word faerie out with yokai and therefore asking why you'd need any sort of particular seeming/kith to represent something that could be represented more or less by the whole darn template by itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T14:27:05-07:00","id":496783,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I went back and edited it after giving it some thought. They do sound more appropriate for a Seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T14:57:21-07:00","id":496801,"title":"","content":"Here are some interpretations I was able to come up with for Kiths regarding this potential seeming.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fireheart</b> - Changed into paper lanterns known as Burabura, these Yokai appear colorful and delicate to the touch. They have a tendency to wear tassels or strips of kanji hanging off their bodies and their insides glow with candle light for those who can see through their mask.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Gravewright</b> - Also known as the Dorotabo, these Yokai are recruited from the ranks of country folk, such as farmers. They dwell among lands with a history of abuse, neglect and violence. Where angry spirits or tormented ghosts are likely to be found. They might have the appearance of a long dead farmhand, their clothes still covered in dirt and in a state of disrepair from years of hard labor in the fields.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Brewer</b> - Known as the Kameosa, these Yokai appear to be fashioned out of some manner of clay, plastic or porcelain. In Arcadia, they were used as jars to contain the alcoholic beverages of their Keepers. Their bodily fluids (such as saliva) might give off the smell or even taste of sake to those willing to try it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-29-2015, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T15:17:48-07:00","id":496815,"title":"","content":"So a beast leechfinger would look like its got squid like skin, with fine tentacles for hair, a suckers along its arms. It would be able to heal by draining health from living humanish beings or used that health to gain the hardy merit. They also be able to regain a point of clarity by violating a human taboo. Cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T17:37:09-07:00","id":496910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=496778#post496778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not a hundred percent sure how a wide selection of various spirit/fairy/monsters counts as a Kith, but then again I'm having trouble doing anything other than swapping the word faerie out with yokai and therefore asking why you'd need any sort of particular seeming/kith to represent something that could be represented more or less by the whole darn template by itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. There are hundreds of yokai, and they pretty much all map to existing Seeming/Kith combinations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T18:57:18-07:00","id":496955,"title":"","content":"So wait... If all seeming blessings deal with regaining Clarity, can Fairest not inherently super charge their social charm anymore?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T19:17:17-07:00","id":496965,"title":"","content":"I think that the Contracts will answer this - remeber that new Contracts will have stracture quasi-like Werewolf Gifts - there will be one thematic power to each Seeming, like Uratha are having one per Renown. So the Fairest will have powers to look and be more beutifull most of the time, beside their basic Seeming Blessing.<br /> <br /> I have other question concerned on the Seemings now - from the Kiths spoiled document it seems that new Wizned are Franskenstein-like their own body parts exchangers for mechanical components. But what about all the fairy tales dwarves, gnomes, pixies and all this &quot;<i>Little People hard working thier magic</i>&quot; that Wizened were in 1ed? Basiclly, who will now have mine True Fae Santa Clause in this slaverish toy factory as &quot;worker elves&quot;, hmm? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T19:25:46-07:00","id":496971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=496955#post496955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So wait... If all seeming blessings deal with regaining Clarity, can Fairest not inherently super charge their social charm anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that'd be by default anymore. It feels like most of the inherent, non-Contract powers that aren't universal to all Changelings will be coming from Kiths, which are quite a bit more potent and robust in 2e. If you want a Changeling who can inherently supercharge their social charms, you'd need to pick a Kith that's good at that, and then take whatever Seeming you please.<br /> <br /> That said, I have two points: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Is the Beast Seeming writeup we've seen the complete one? I presume so, but if a Seeming gives anything other than a Blessing and Curse, there could be room for some such inherent perk.</li> <li>Last we heard about Contracts, most of them will have a few Seeming versions (clauses?) for an extra effect, power, or application. If you're a member of that Seeming, you get it free when you buy the Contract. If the Fairest's versions are often more social-focused than most others, that might contribute to the idea of them being potent socialites, relative to the other Seemings.</li> </ol><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T19:38:04-07:00","id":496977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=496965#post496965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the Contracts will answer this - remeber that new Contracts will have stracture quasi-like Werewolf Gifts - there will be one thematic power to each Seeming, like Uratha are having one per Renown. So the Fairest will have powers to look and be more beutifull most of the time, beside their basic Seeming Blessing.<br /> <br /> I have other question concerned on the Seemings now - from the Kiths spoiled document it seems that new Wizned are Franskenstein-like their own body parts exchangers for mechanical components. But what about all the fairy tales dwarves, gnomes, pixies and all this &quot;<i>Little People hard working thier magic</i>&quot; that Wizened were in 1ed? Basiclly, who will now have mine True Fae Santa Clause in this slaverish toy factory as &quot;worker elves&quot;, hmm? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Just imagine the Santa Elves have hammers and screwdrivers for hands. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Or you could just make them be Smiths, since that's pretty much what they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T19:40:28-07:00","id":496978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=496971#post496971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Is the Beast Seeming writeup we've seen the complete one? I presume so, but if a Seeming gives anything other than a Blessing and Curse, there could be room for some such inherent perk.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> No, there are going to be roughly 100 Kiths in the core book, and I believe they said that write up A) only covered a third of them, and B) was a first draft. So more will be added / tweaked in the future.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T19:56:17-07:00","id":497013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=496978#post496978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, there are going to be roughly 100 Kiths in the core book, and I believe they said that write up A) only covered a third of them, and B) was a first draft. So more will be added / tweaked in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>While this is true, I think you may have meant to quote someone else. I know that all Changelings have a Kith Blessing, and Changelings with a Seeming also have Seeming Contract affinities, a Seeming Blessing, and a Seeming Curse. My question was about whether the Beast Seeming writeup we saw was complete, or if it might have been intentionally holding back one or more additional things a Seeming might provide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T20:06:34-07:00","id":497019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=496977#post496977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just imagine the Santa Elves have hammers and screwdrivers for hands. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Or you could just make them be Smiths, since that's pretty much what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine the Santa's Elves would be Smiths Fairest - they are so preatty and do so wonderfull toys! Even when chained to the factory tables. Awwww... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But back to game design reality - still, there are many fae stories about &quot;Little People&quot; making things. And all the legends of dwarves, gnomes and others beings. All them are Smiths? This would make like Kith being as large as Seeming almost. Or maybe Smiths, and for example, Little Ones and Pixies Kiths represent archetype? &quot;Small Men&quot; are big fea-ish theme in folklore. Or just a Small-Framed Merit is <b>very, very, VERY</b> popular in <b>CtL</b> 2ED setting? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T21:06:08-07:00","id":497065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=497013#post497013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While this is true, I think you may have meant to quote someone else. I know that all Changelings have a Kith Blessing, and Changelings with a Seeming also have Seeming Contract affinities, a Seeming Blessing, and a Seeming Curse. My question was about whether the Beast Seeming writeup we saw was complete, or if it might have been intentionally holding back one or more additional things a Seeming might provide.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Woops, I misread your quote earlier. Sorry about that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"J