padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9hTpUAabSMM\" data-code=\"9hTpUAabSMM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/9hTpUAabSMM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T22:49:26-07:00","id":497115,"title":"","content":"Oh, youkai have been brought up! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That really makes me want to play one of those in 2nd edition now! I've always had a place in my heart for the mischeavious and lascivious Kappa myself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So to keep roughly on-topic with Seemings rather than Kiths, of which I shall talk more in the relevant thread... I noticed a common theme with the Wizened in that they seemed to have artificial parts and seemed more 'clockwork man' this time around. It makes me wonder just what a person needs to do to get that Seeming...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T23:21:59-07:00","id":497130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=496752#post496752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hmm, after first going through the Wiki, I was thinking they sounded like a Kith, but another look through showed they have a wide number of capabilities, so a Seeming does seem appropriate.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Yokai are honestly too broad a concept to even be a Seeming. I mean, it's pretty much as broad a concept as &quot;Faerie&quot; is - just a different culture's conception thereof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T23:34:01-07:00","id":497134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=497130#post497130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yokai are honestly too broad a concept to even be a Seeming. I mean, it's pretty much as broad a concept as &quot;Faerie&quot; is - just a different culture's conception thereof.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would make for a fantastic setting book, though. There's too many informed cultural idioms in the concept of a &quot;Youkai&quot; to really compress it into a kith or seeming and do the concept justice. One thing that'd also be wonderful would be something along the lines of the Australian Aboriginal Dreaming. Same thing, too many cultural mores to compress into a single thing but would make for an amazing setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T23:49:55-07:00","id":497162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=497134#post497134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would make for a fantastic setting book, though. There's too many informed cultural idioms in the concept of a &quot;Youkai&quot; to really compress it into a kith or seeming and do the concept justice. One thing that'd also be wonderful would be something along the lines of the Australian Aboriginal Dreaming. Same thing, too many cultural mores to compress into a single thing but would make for an amazing setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Individual types of Youkai are fairly easy to express with a Kith and Seeming, though. Yuki-ona? An Ice-kith paired with Fairest or Elemental. Kitsune? A trickster Kith paired with the Beast Seeming. Oni? Any kith paired with Ogre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T05:15:46-07:00","id":497333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=497130#post497130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yokai are honestly too broad a concept to even be a Seeming. I mean, it's pretty much as broad a concept as &quot;Faerie&quot; is - just a different culture's conception thereof.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Maybe they could be interpreted as &quot;Eastern Fae&quot; just as the Hengeyokai were Eastern Lycanthropes. <br /> <br /> Kappas have a pretty nice life, villagers give them all the cucumbers they could want, and when they're ticked off, they'll rip your soul out through your ass, literally!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T06:47:21-07:00","id":497402,"title":"","content":"I wonder if there's a kith who gives up something physical to escape. Could work for elements, who meld something beyond flesh into their bodies during the escape","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T06:50:52-07:00","id":497403,"title":"","content":"Wizened - they look like they change parts of their body to make themselves something other than original role of Kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T08:31:22-07:00","id":497466,"title":"","content":"So, Beasts! Curiouser and curiouser, I must say. <br /> <br /> One thing that I am absolutely adoring is the shift from Beast = dumb of the first game. I actually feel more inclined to play a Beast now than I did ever before. The breaking-of-social-taboos does seem more animalistic; animals aren't human, don't think like them. Humans have to think like them. <br /> <br /> The rest, however, I really feel like its either a repeat of the themes from 1e (which, while good to see, I can't get excited about), or we're missing pieces. The escape thing feels odd to me as it is - is the extra glamour to reflect freaking out more? I feel like something's missing, but I can't tell without the other rule set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T08:38:51-07:00","id":497497,"title":"","content":"Seriously, Yokai* are Faeries. It's simple.<br /> <br /> *Need to look up the word again, see if it has a u or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T08:42:28-07:00","id":497499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=497497#post497497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, Yokai* are Faeries. It's simple.<br /> <br /> *Need to look up the word again, see if it has a u or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a long &quot;o&quot; and Japanese has historically been all over the place with what the &quot;correct&quot; way to romanize those is, but standard practice and transliteration in Hepburn is to use the &quot;u.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T10:38:43-07:00","id":497627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=497402#post497402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if there's a kith who gives up something physical to escape. Could work for elements, who meld something beyond flesh into their bodies during the escape</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that this is a game about emotions, I feel like &quot;gives up something physical&quot; is a fairly boring notion for a Seeming. Rather, I'd prefer it if the &quot;something physical&quot; was an emotional touchstone of some kind and <i>that's</i> what they give up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T11:37:23-07:00","id":497663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=494858#post494858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part about the &quot;transformation in details&quot; I get - the outlook change. I do not get <b>logic</b> of it. HOW becoming more like animal your Keeper wanted you to be, can help you to free for him? You make <b>exactly</b> what he wanted to do you into first place. HOW becoming beautyfull wolf can free you? Even becoming Shadow Wolf. You are still A WOLF the Keeper wanted you to be, don't you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Keeper wanted a <i>pet</i> wolf. When you take on the Beast Seeming you become a <i>wild</i> wolf and are beyond his control. When you take on the Elemental Seeming you (at a guess) learn the lay of the land as only a wolf can and escape him via a route he can't follow. When you take on the Ogre Seeming you turn on him - he wanted a wolf, but wolves can bite and harry. When you take on the Fairest Seeming - ok, that one is more of a stretch, but you dazzle him and he can't bring himself to keep you, maybe. When you take on the Darkling Seeming, you become one with the night, as wolves should be, and escape through darkness he can't penetrate. When you take on the Wizened Seeming, you (again at a guess) become a <i>dog</i> - and dogs understand the owner's world better than wolves ever can, so you escape through corners of his world he could never have expected you to spot.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T14:33:41-07:00","id":497887,"title":"","content":"Already gave the wolf example, Sunless. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> I was thinking that a Fairest wolf could be a majestic and beautiful creature of the wilderness. Imagine that white wolf (hah) from the Balto movie.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ucfHDO4k9gM\" data-code=\"ucfHDO4k9gM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ucfHDO4k9gM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-30-2015, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T17:05:05-07:00","id":497998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=497663#post497663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you take on the Wizened Seeming, you (again at a guess) become a <i>dog</i> - and dogs understand the owner's world better than wolves ever can, so you escape through corners of his world he could never have expected you to spot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like this to Wizened - being &quot;smaller&quot; after your expiriance in Arcadia was very interesting to me, as all the stroies of dwarves, gnomes, pixies or even &quot;you lost all your youth in those wretched chambers&quot;. But the Kiths Sample marks, mostly, that 2ed Wizeneds are replacing parts of their body, to become something Frankenstein-like and by this defy their Keepers role. To what it is, I have a mixed feelings - I love Frankensteins in <b>Promethean</b> and I definitly can see some mechanics augumented beings treated as 'alien' to mortals. But on the other hand exchanging your body parts do not strike me as something very &quot;fea-like&quot;. And our Wolf changeling from example should be Frankenstein-like amalgat of wolf parts as Wizened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-30-2015, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T17:50:22-07:00","id":498045,"title":"","content":"While I agree that cyborg implants doesn't exactly sound very Fae, the 1e Wizened were primarily used as the labor force of the Changelings. They made shoes, prepared meals, played music, brewed drinks, est. Their major role in Arcadia was to perform menial tasks and chores. That being said, it makes sense that in 2e, they would have the tools of their trade integrated into their body.<br /> <br /> <b>In fact, imagine this scenario:</b> The Wizened is constantly observed by the overbearing servants of their Keeper. They can't make an escape during work hours, so they instead choose to break out later that night, when the workers have gone to sleep. With slight of hand, plus the magic of Arcadia fueling them, they manage to smuggle their tools away from the work station, and thus use them to escape once the coast is clear. Except Arcadia saw that they were concealing these tools on their person and reconstructed their bodies accordingly, now the tools are part of them, hidden inside compartments or pockets where they can be stored when not in use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T18:34:44-07:00","id":498077,"title":"","content":"I think that, if we're going to get another Seeming spoiled, I would want to see Wizened spoiled. I love the descriptions of their tools in their bodies, it's SO evocative, but I don't quite get the fairy-tale aspect of it. I'm not SCEPTICAL per se, more just interested to see how they're going to pull it off (in full confidence that they will).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T18:56:32-07:00","id":498090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=498077#post498077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that, if we're going to get another Seeming spoiled, I would want to see Wizened spoiled. I love the descriptions of their tools in their bodies, it's SO evocative, but I don't quite get the fairy-tale aspect of it. I'm not SCEPTICAL per se, more just interested to see how they're going to pull it off (in full confidence that they will).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll probably end up posting all of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T19:21:08-07:00","id":498117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=498045#post498045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree that cyborg implants doesn't exactly sound very Fae, the 1e Wizened were primarily used as the labor force of the Changelings. They made shoes, prepared meals, played music, brewed drinks, est. Their major role in Arcadia was to perform menial tasks and chores. That being said, it makes sense that in 2e, they would have the tools of their trade integrated into their body.<br /> <br /> <b>In fact, imagine this scenario:</b> The Wizened is constantly observed by the overbearing servants of their Keeper. They can't make an escape during work hours, so they instead choose to break out later that night, when the workers have gone to sleep. With slight of hand, plus the magic of Arcadia fueling them, they manage to smuggle their tools away from the work station, and thus use them to escape once the coast is clear. Except Arcadia saw that they were concealing these tools on their person and reconstructed their bodies accordingly, now the tools are part of them, hidden inside compartments or pockets where they can be stored when not in use.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would much more like to mark <b><i>The Loss</i></b> as Wizened theme. This would about replacing your limbs with other things, but also shrinking on the whole hours you worked over to free yourself ( like secretly saw the chains are hanging you to the workstation ) or losing most years and vitality doing your Keepers wishes. You could ended with mixed body parts or being very wretched or hag-like looking. That way we could have Frankenstein-like amalgations Kiths + Wizened combination when it's logical and &quot;affected by life&quot; when it's not. And still, both options seem logical inside a Seeming.<br /> <br /> Having Wizened as guys with tools instead of they hands - many times - looks weird. No, change it - unfairy tale. And it's bad in the games about faieris, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> Like with our Wolf changeling example - becoming the dog is <i>loss of status</i> as the being. And it's somehow suitable to the spirit of 1ed Wizened. Making our Wolf mixed corpses zombie is just... unthematic. And still should be rather covered by the Darklings, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-30-2015, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T20:22:26-07:00","id":498153,"title":"","content":"The last part of your post is confusing (likely a result of a poor translating program), but what do you mean about a wolf made of mixed corpses?<br /> <br /> On another note, I can see the logic behind the Wizened becoming 'wizened' as a result of sweat shop labor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T00:40:38-07:00","id":498459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=498153#post498153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last part of your post is confusing (likely a result of a poor translating program), but what do you mean about a wolf made of mixed corpses?</div> </div> </div> </div>I will use D&amp;D image here...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://cdn.obsidianportal.com/assets/203383/Flesh_Golem_Hound.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://cdn.obsidianportal.com/assets...olem_Hound.jpg</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/489043-second-edition-beasts?p=498153#post498153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note, I can see the logic behind the Wizened becoming 'wizened' as a result of sweat shop labor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also, but not all the time. Theme should work with word meaning AND game logic.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/wizen\" target=\"_blank\">Mariam-Webster Directory</a> says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Definition of WIZEN</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#757575\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:14px\">intransitive verb</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#223645\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">to become dry, shrunken, and wrinkled often as a result of aging or of failing vitality</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Being &quot;sweat shoped&quot; can be wizened, but so do becoming &quot;scarred&quot; by your work in general. And like I said before - not always exchanging body parts is very fea-like. Sometimes going with &quot;wrinkeled, small men&quot; would be much more appropiate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T06:26:18-07:00","id":498757,"title":"","content":"New Kith Out, everybody jump over to Darklings! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T07:05:48-07:00","id":498797,"title":"","content":"You mean Seeming, not kith :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T07:27:35-07:00","id":498813,"title":"","content":"Was about to come edit this. Once I realized that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""}